'' =================================================================================================
''
''   File....... util_adopt_motor.spin2
''   Purpose.... The motor-adoption tool: measure a motor's commutation offsets (the hall zero Z and the lead,
''               from each direction's current minimum) and its speed ceiling (the duty reserve), from that
''               motor's parameter record
''   Authors.... Stephen M Moraco
''               -- Copyright (c) 2026 Iron Sheep Productions, LLC
''               -- see below for terms of use
''   E-mail..... stephen@ironsheep.biz
''   Started.... 04 Oct 2026
''   Updated.... 04 Oct 2026
''               04 Oct 2026 -- task 3695 (TOOL_REV 2): the ladder's rung loops are REPEAT nRungs WITH idx (FROM 0 TO
''               nRungs - 1 runs twice at nRungs = 0). A record that refuses its plan never reaches them; no record changes.
''               06 Oct 2026 -- PL-207 (TOOL_REV 3): the DocoEng record's scan and ladder limits are the library's 40 A,
''               as the measuring harness's are (they were 2 and 3 A, at which this motor's own scan hunted and drooped
''               on Rev A). No output format changes.
''               07 Oct 2026 -- PL-209 (TOOL_REV 4): a scan side also ends FIT_HALF_DEG past its lowest clean point
''               (MA-SIDE end,BRACKETED): at 40 A every Doco side walked on into the torque wall and over-current. A
''               new end token; no field changes.
''
'' =================================================================================================

{ WHAT IT DOES

  ADDING_MOTOR.md steps 5 and 6, run for you: with your motor free to turn and nothing touching it, the tool
   1. finds your motor's PARAMETER RECORD (DAT { motor records }, below) by the MOTOR_TYPE your configuration names,
      and refuses -- before anything is started -- a motor type with no record, a record of another layout, or a
      record whose hall ticks per revolution disagree with the driver's;
   2. starts the motor with its start checks, under the record's test current limit, and reads the current sense's
      rest zero;
   3. THE OFFSETS (step 5): at the record's two scan speeds, one octave apart, for negative and then positive
      increments, steps the commutation offset that direction uses 5 degrees at a time, outward from the pair the
      driver starts with, one side at a time, each side from rest, until the motor reaches an edge (below); fits a
      parabola to the DC-link current around the lowest point; and gives each direction's current minimum, their
      midpoint Z (the hall zero) and half their difference L (the lead). Z must not move with speed: the tool
      checks it does not;
   4. puts back the commutation the driver started with;
   5. THE CEILING (step 6): for each increment sign, climbs a ladder of speeds on that commutation until the duty
      reaches 92.5 % of the drive's duty ceiling (7.5 % in hand) or an edge, fits the duty line, and gives the
      increment at the reserve -- the number confgurePowerLimits() takes;
   6. stops the motor and prints MA-RESULT: the pair to put in offsetsForMotor() and the ceiling to put in
      confgurePowerLimits(), for the voltage you started it at.
  Run it once: put the pair in, rebuild, and run it again. The second run measures the ceiling on YOUR pair, and its
  minima should then sit at the pair it started from (MA-FIT from_start_x10 near 0).

  WHERE IT RUNS, AND WHY HERE. It is a top-level program you compile under your own configuration
  (isp_bldc_motor_userconfig.spin2, the single-motor block) and run from the debug terminal, because that is what the
  reader of ADDING_MOTOR.md has: their own motor, one board, their configuration file, pnut-ts and the debug terminal --
  and, in general, no shaft encoder. So it measures only what the board itself can see: the halls, the DC-link current
  and the drive's own counters. Our bench runs this same source (tools/bench-run.sh doco-adopt-<voltage> on the Doco
  bench, adopt-wheel on one 6.5in wheel); the bench's shaft encoder judges the tool there from outside, through the
  bench's own measurement harness (test_bench_single.spin2). Nothing here needs the encoder, and no bench file is
  needed to build it.

  THE MOTOR RECORD (record format 1, RECORD_FORMAT). One record per motor type, REC_LONGS longs, in this order; the
  table ends with a record whose key is END_OF_RECORDS:
    key             the motor's name, from the list in isp_bldc_motor_userconfig.spin2 (an alias in CON { record keys })
    format          RECORD_FORMAT: a record written for another layout is refused
    status          RS_MEASURED (every number below measured on that motor), or RS_PROVISIONAL (some come from the data
                    sheet or a model and are still to be measured: MA-RECORD and MA-RESULT say so)
    ticks_rev       hall ticks per revolution, counted by hand (ADDING_MOTOR.md step 3); must equal the driver's own
    rated_ma        the motor's rated current, mA: the absolute current abort is twice it
    no_load_ma      the motor's no-load current, mA: the current wall's floor, and the charge allowance per second driven
    scan_a          the test current limit for the offset scan, whole amps (peak and continuous)
    ladder_a        the test current limit for the ceiling ladder, whole amps
    slow_rpm        the slower offset-scan speed, rpm ...
    fast_rpm        ... and the faster, about twice it: Z is measured at both and must agree
    ladder_from_rpm the ladder's first rung, rpm ...
    ladder_step_rpm ... the step between rungs ...
    ladder_to_rpm   ... and the fastest rung it may ever command: the climb stops at the duty reserve or an edge first
  To adopt a new motor, add its name to CON { record keys } and one record above the END_OF_RECORDS line, in this
  layout, from its data sheet and step 3's count; mark it RS_PROVISIONAL until a run has confirmed it.

  THE EDGE -- where a side of the offset scan, or the ladder's climb, stops. A motor tells the drive it is out of its
  working range in different ways, and the tool stops on any of them:
    WALL   the DC link stays over max(2.5 x the side's lowest clean point so far, no_load_ma) for 40 readings (200 ms),
           or over 80 % of the absolute abort for 4: too much lead, the current explodes (the 6.5in's offset scans ended
           there; the offset scan only -- on the ladder the absolute abort stands guard)
    DROOP  the motor turns at under 80 % of the commanded speed, on the halls: too little lead, it cannot make the
           torque and slows (the 6.5in's torque wall: it droops rather than faults)
    HUNT   the drive held the field back (a held pass) while the rotor lagged: the DocoEng motor is predicted to hunt
           before it slows, 20-30 degrees ahead of its minimum (from our desk model; not yet measured)
    FAULT  the driver faulted (the DocoEng motor is predicted to fault, not slip, above an increment of 419e6)
    CAPPED the duty hit its ceiling (the ladder only: the knee, past the reserve)
  WALL and FAULT end a side at once; DROOP and HUNT after two points in a row (a single rough point does not). Until a
  side has seen a clean point, a DROOP or HUNT point drawing less current than the one before does not count: the walk
  is still coming down toward a minimum it has not reached, which it must be allowed to do when the driver's starting
  pair sits in the hunting region. A ladder rung that DROOPs, HUNTs, CAPs or FAULTs ends the climb at once. No rung, and no scan speed, passes an increment
  of PK1_CAP_INCR: above it one drive pass moves the field further than the driver's lag margin allows, so a
  disturbance faults instead of slipping.

  THE CHECKS -- each prints its verdict; none drives anything.
    RECORD    PRECONDITION nothing started. BOUND a record whose key is MOTOR_TYPE, whose format is RECORD_FORMAT, and
              whose ticks_rev equals hallTicInfoForMotor(). CORRECT CASE the 6.5in and the DocoEng records are found;
              any other motor type is refused NO_RECORD. Rival: the driver's own refusal of an unknown motor (start()),
              which would come later and name the motor, not the missing record.
    FIT       per scan speed and direction. PRECONDITION at least FIT_MIN_PTS clean points (finished their window,
              following within 3 %, no held pass, no re-sync) within FIT_HALF_DEG of the lowest. BOUND curvature above 0,
              the vertex inside the points fitted, and the vertex's own standard error at most VERT_SE_MAX_X10 / 10
              degrees. CORRECT CASE a basin like the 6.5in's (13.1 mV at its minimum, 12.7x that 30 degrees away)
              resolves to within a degree of its lowest point. Unfixed value: the 2.5 degree bound, derived for the
              DocoEng on Rev A's current resolution and not yet tried on a measured curve. Rival: a "minimum" pinned
              against an edge with nothing measured beyond it -- refused by the inside-the-points rule.
    Z         PRECONDITION both directions' fits resolved at both speeds. BOUND Z at the two speeds within
              Z_AGREE_TOL_X10 / 10 degrees. CORRECT CASE the 6.5in's Z moved 0.2-0.55 degrees across a doubling of speed
              while its lead moved 12 degrees. Unfixed value: 7.5 degrees, three of the fit's own standard errors
              (2.5 degrees each way), until the two motors' runs show their spread. Rival: a lead that changes with
              speed -- it cancels in the midpoint, so it cannot fail this check; a minimum found against an edge, or
              the wrong minimum, can.
    CEILING   per increment sign. PRECONDITION at least two clean rungs and a rising duty line. BOUND the climb ends on
              the reserve -- a clean rung at DUTY_RESERVE_PM of the duty ceiling, the duty line's crossing then at or
              below the fastest clean rung (bracketed) -- or on an edge or the field-step margin with a clean rung below
              it; NOT FOUND when the rungs ran out first (ladder_to too low), the climb never drove, or no rung was
              clean. The ceiling is the reserve crossing, or the fastest clean rung below whatever came first. CORRECT
              CASE the 6.5in at 18.5 V: 165e6, where duty runs at 92-93 % of its ceiling. Unfixed value: the reserve,
              925 per mille, the 6.5in's, carried to every motor. Rival: an edge before the reserve (the motor cannot
              use the voltage it is given) -- MA-CEILING names it, and the line's own crossing prints beside it.

  THE GUARDS, because nobody need watch it. Every 5 ms while the motor is driven:
    - an absolute current abort at twice the record's rated current, on 4 readings in a row: the motor coasts and the
      run ends;
    - a charge cap: a minute at the rated current, plus the no-load current over the run's estimated driven time;
    - a time cap: three times the run's estimated length;
    - a driver fault is a finding: the motor is brought to rest, the fault cleared, and the scan or climb goes on from
      rest; a fault that will not clear ends the run.
  Before anything moves: start() with its start checks refusing (a disconnected lead, a hall fault, no board); the
  record's test current limit set and read back (testSetCurrentLimits()); the current sense's rest zero inside the
  driver's band for the board it detected; every scan speed and rung under PK1_CAP_INCR. At rest the shaft coasts. The
  motor is stopped on every way out. PANIC: disconnect the supply.

  WHAT IT PRINTS (record format FMT_VERSION). One line per record, tag first, then name,value pairs; every record
  prints every field in the same order, NA where nothing was measured; at most 280 bytes. Directions are named by the
  increment sign (NEG: offsetsForMotor()'s fwdDegrees; POS: its revDegrees), never "forward". Angles are electrical
  degrees, _x10 fields tenths of a degree; currents mA of DC link; speeds rpm. Nothing prints while the motor turns.
    MA-BANNER, MA-RECORD, MA-REFUSE, MA-PLAN, MA-START, MA-LIMIT, MA-ZERO      what was built, the record, the start
    MA-POINT, MA-SIDE, MA-FIT, MA-PAIR, MA-ZCHECK, MA-RESTORE                  the offset scan
    MA-RUNG, MA-CEILING                                                        the ceiling ladder
    MA-RESULT, MA-END                                                          what to put in the driver; how it ended

  HOW IT IS RUN. Name your motor in the single-motor block of isp_bldc_motor_userconfig.spin2 (MOTOR_TYPE,
  ONLY_MOTOR_BASE, DRIVE_VOLTAGE, ONLY_BOARD_TYPE), then from src/:
      pnut-ts -d util_adopt_motor.spin2
      pnut-term-ts -r util_adopt_motor.bin
  About 15-30 minutes per voltage, unattended.
}

' Select the single-motor configuration in isp_bldc_motor_userconfig.spin2 (a -D BENCH_CFG build uses the bench file instead)
#DEFINE CFG_SINGLE_MOTOR
#IFDEF __PNUT_TS__
#PRAGMA EXPORTDEF CFG_SINGLE_MOTOR
#ENDIF

CON { timing }

    CLK_FREQ = 270_000_000                                  ' tools/bench-run.sh sets this line to a clock chosen by NAME
    _clkfreq = CLK_FREQ

CON { tool identity }

    TOOL_REV        = 4                                     ' this source's revision (4: a side ends BRACKETED, PL-209; 3:the DocoEng record at 40 A, PL-207; 2: counted loops are REPEAT n WITH idx, task 3695)
    FMT_VERSION     = 1                                     ' the MA- record format
    RECORD_FORMAT   = 1                                     ' the motor record's layout (CON { the motor record })

OBJ { the motor, its configuration, the record builder }

#ifdef BENCH_CFG
    user     : "isp_bldc_motor_userconfig_bench"            ' our bench's fixed statement (-D BENCH_CFG, tools/bench-run.sh)
#else
    user     : "isp_bldc_motor_userconfig"                  ' your configuration: the single-motor block
#endif
    wheel    : "isp_bldc_motor"                             ' the one motor
    benchLog : "isp_bench_log"                              ' the record builder: one debug() line per record

CON { the motor this tool measures }

  ' Your build reads the single-motor block (ONLY_*). Our two benches: the Doco bench names one motor too; the 6.5in
  '  platform is two wheels, so the tool drives its RIGHT wheel (the P16 board), as the single-motor demo does there.
    #0, BUILD_USER, BUILD_DOCO_BENCH, BUILD_WHEEL_BENCH
#ifdef BENCH_DOCO
    MOTOR_BASE          = user.ONLY_MOTOR_BASE
    MOTOR_BOARD_TYPE    = user.ONLY_BOARD_TYPE
    BUILD_KIND          = BUILD_DOCO_BENCH
#elseifdef BENCH_CFG
    MOTOR_BASE          = user.RIGHT_MOTOR_BASE
    MOTOR_BOARD_TYPE    = user.RIGHT_BOARD_TYPE
    BUILD_KIND          = BUILD_WHEEL_BENCH
#else
    MOTOR_BASE          = user.ONLY_MOTOR_BASE
    MOTOR_BOARD_TYPE    = user.ONLY_BOARD_TYPE
    BUILD_KIND          = BUILD_USER
#endif

CON { the motor record -- layout, record format 1 }

    #0, REC_KEY, REC_FORMAT, REC_STATUS, REC_TICKS_PER_REV, REC_RATED_MA, REC_NO_LOAD_MA, REC_SCAN_A, REC_LADDER_A, ...
        REC_SLOW_RPM, REC_FAST_RPM, REC_LADDER_FROM_RPM, REC_LADDER_STEP_RPM, REC_LADDER_TO_RPM, REC_LONGS
    #0, RS_MEASURED, RS_PROVISIONAL
    END_OF_RECORDS      = -1                                ' the key of the record that ends the table
    RECORDS_MAX         = 16                                ' the table walk's bound

CON { record keys -- one per motor that has a record }

    KEY_6_5_INCH        = user.MOTR_6_5_INCH
    KEY_DOCO_4KRPM      = user.MOTR_DOCO_4KRPM

CON { the procedure -- the same for every motor }

  ' Readings and windows (the measurement harnesses' own: a reading every 5 ms; at each point or rung 1 s to settle,
  '  then a 5 s window, which resolves a Rev A board's DC link to about 10 mA where one reading is +-600 mA)
    SAMPLE_MS           = 5
    ZERO_SAMPLES        = 200                               ' the rest zero: 200 readings, 1 s
    ZERO_SPREAD_MIN_MV  = 1                                 ' a live current sense's readings differ
    SETTLE_MS           = 1_000
    WINDOW_MS           = 5_000
    REST_MS             = 500                               ' at rest between drives
    READY_TIMEOUT_MS    = 2_000
    READY_POLL_MS       = 2
    ARRIVE_MAX_MS       = 15_000                            ' a speed change's bound: the built-in ramp reaches any ceiling in 9 s
    STOP_MAX_MS         = 15_000                            ' a stop's bound: the built-in ramp stops from any ceiling in 6 s
    SAMPLES_PER_SEC     = 1_000 / SAMPLE_MS

  ' The offset scan: 5 degree steps (both motors' scans), out to 90 degrees from the start pair at most; the fit window
  '  20 degrees either side of the lowest clean point (the 6.5in scan's fine window)
    OFS_STEP_DEG        = 5
    OFS_SIDE_STEPS      = 18                                ' 18 x 5 = 90 degrees
    OFS_SIDE_POINTS     = OFS_SIDE_STEPS + 1
    OFS_POINTS          = 2 * OFS_SIDE_POINTS
    FIT_HALF_DEG        = 20
    FIT_MIN_PTS         = 5
    VERT_SE_MAX_X10     = 25                                ' the vertex's standard error, tenths of a degree
    Z_AGREE_TOL_X10     = 75                                ' Z at the two speeds, tenths of a degree

  ' The edge (the header's THE EDGE)
    WALL_REL_X100       = 250                               ' 2.5 x the side's first point ...
    WALL_REL_SAMPLES    = 40                                ' ... for 200 ms
    WALL_CEIL_PCT       = 80                                ' 80 % of the absolute abort ...
    ABS_ABORT_SAMPLES   = 4                                 ' ... (and the abort itself) for 20 ms
    DROOP_PM            = 800                               ' turning at under 80 % of the command
    HUNT_HELD_MIN       = 1                                 ' a held pass in a window
    EDGE_RUN            = 2                                 ' DROOP or HUNT points in a row that end a side
    FOLLOW_TOL_PM       = 30                                ' a clean point or rung follows within 3 %

  ' The ceiling: the 6.5in's duty reserve, 92.5 % of the duty ceiling; and the field-step margin no command passes
    DUTY_RESERVE_PM     = 925
    PK1_CAP_INCR        = 419_000_000
    RUNGS_MAX           = 40

  ' The guards
    ABORT_X_RATED       = 2                                 ' the absolute abort: twice the rated current
    CHARGE_RATED_S      = 60                                ' the charge cap's base: a minute at the rated current
    TIME_FACTOR         = 3                                 ' the time cap: three times the estimated run
    EST_CHANGE_S        = 10                                ' the estimate's allowance for a speed-up or a stop
    EST_STEP_S          = 3                                 ' ... and for a step between rungs

  ' Scales
    PM                  = 1_000                             ' per mille
    X10                 = 10
    X100                = 100
    TENTHS_PER_TURN     = wheel.TENTHS_PER_TURN             ' a turn of a commutation offset, tenths of a degree
    F_2POW32            = 4294967296.0
    SECS_PER_MIN        = 60

CON { enums }

    #0, SIGN_NEG, SIGN_POS
    #0, SIDE_PLUS, SIDE_MINUS
    #0, SPEED_SLOW, SPEED_FAST
    SPEEDS              = 2
    SIGNS               = 2

  ' a point's or a rung's outcome
    #0, PO_NOT_RUN, PO_SKIPPED, PO_CLEAN, PO_ROUGH, PO_DROOP, PO_HUNT, PO_CAPPED, PO_WALL, PO_FAULT, PO_STOPPED, ...
        PO_START, PO_BOUND
  ' why a side or a climb ended (PO_* where an edge ended it; these where nothing did)
    END_LIMIT           = 100                               ' a side reached its 90 degrees
    END_RESERVE         = 101                               ' a climb reached the duty reserve
    END_TOP             = 102                               ' a climb ran its last rung below the reserve
    END_BRACKETED       = 103                               ' PL-209 (TOOL_REV 4): a side reached FIT_HALF_DEG past its lowest clean point

  ' a sampler reading's outcome
    #0, GO_RUNNING, GO_FAULT, GO_OVER_CURRENT, GO_CHARGE_CAP, GO_TIME_CAP

  ' waitPhase()'s conditions, and its outcome
    #0, UNTIL_ARRIVED, UNTIL_STOPPED, UNTIL_ELAPSED
    #0, RO_DONE, RO_TIMEOUT, RO_FAULT, RO_STOPPED, RO_REFUSED

  ' why the run ended early or never started (the first cause is kept)
    #0, AR_NONE, AR_NO_RECORD, AR_RECORD_FORMAT, AR_GEOMETRY, AR_RECORD_PLAN, AR_CONFIG, AR_START, AR_BOARD, ...
        AR_LIMIT, AR_ZERO, AR_OVER_CURRENT, AR_CHARGE_CAP, AR_TIME_CAP, AR_FAULT_STUCK, AR_STOP_TIMEOUT, AR_RESTORE

  ' a check's verdict
    #0, VD_NA, VD_PASS, VD_FAIL

  ' record field widths
    LIM_TINY            = benchLog.LIM_TINY
    LIM_SMALL           = benchLog.LIM_SMALL
    LIM_MID             = benchLog.LIM_MID
    LIM_BIG             = benchLog.LIM_BIG
    TOKMAX              = 14                                ' the longest token any field prints

DAT { motor records -- format 1: the layout is the CON block above, and the file's header says what each field means }

  ' THE 6.5in HUB MOTOR. Every number measured on it.
  '  ticks_rev 90: counted by hand, three turns (ADDING_MOTOR.md step 3).
  '  rated_ma 5_000: no vendor rating is on record; twice it is the 10 A absolute abort every 6.5in offset scan ran under.
  '  no_load_ma 500: the pack current of a lifted wheel at the duty knee, 175e6 at 18.5 V (the 6.5in technical manual 6.3).
  '  scan_a / ladder_a 4: the least whole amp over the 2.6 A of DC link the 6.5in's offset scan read at its current wall,
  '   so the limit leaves that wall a current wall.
  '  slow_rpm 33 / fast_rpm 65: 49.5 and 97.5 hall ticks/s, the two speeds its hall zero (-4 degrees) was measured at.
  '  ladder 30 .. 435 rpm in 15 rpm rungs: from under its 6 V ceiling (95 rpm) to 244e6 at 18.5 V, inside the 245e6 it
  '   followed smoothly to, lifted (the manual 6.3); its 18.5 V reserve ceiling, 165e6, is 294 rpm.
motorRecords    LONG    KEY_6_5_INCH, RECORD_FORMAT, RS_MEASURED
                LONG    90, 5_000, 500, 4, 4
                LONG    33, 65, 30, 15, 435
  ' THE DocoEng 4k-rpm MOTOR. PROVISIONAL: from its data sheet (DOCs/DOCOMotor.pdf) and our desk model of it; each
  '  number is set by measuring this motor against a shaft encoder (test_bench_single.spin2), as named.
  '  ticks_rev 24: DOCOENG_MOTOR.md; checked by the hall-map leg's encoder check (1,440 counts per 24 ticks).
  '  rated_ma 1_840 and no_load_ma 400: the data sheet (0.0625 N.m at 0.034 N.m/A; 0.4 A no-load).
  '  scan_a / ladder_a 40: the library's own I_PEAK_A, as the measuring harness has run since its SRC_REV 14 (STEPHEN
  '   2026-10-05 "yes A"); the protection is the tool's absolute abort, twice the rated current. PL-207 (TOOL_REV 3):
  '   they were 2 and 3, the harness's test limits before that change; at 2-3 A on Rev A this motor's crawl-speed phase
  '   current reaches the limit, so 5 degrees off the start a point hunted and the next drooped and no fit resolved
  '   (D2, 2026-10-06: debug_261006-140837 and -161820).
  '  slow_rpm 560 / fast_rpm 1_120: 25 % and 50 % of the 12 V ceiling (335e6), the offset-scan leg's two lower speeds.
  '   Set by the offset-scan leg: its minimum must resolve at both.
  '  ladder 280 .. 2_800 rpm in 140 rpm rungs: 2_800 rpm (419e6) is the field-step margin, which this motor reaches below
  '   its reserve from 12 V up (the model puts 12 V's top, 2_238 rpm, at 71-76 % duty). Set by the ladder leg's duty line.
                LONG    KEY_DOCO_4KRPM, RECORD_FORMAT, RS_PROVISIONAL
                LONG    24, 1_840, 400, 40, 40
                LONG    560, 1_120, 280, 140, 2_800
  ' the end of the table: a new motor's record goes above this line
                LONG    END_OF_RECORDS, 0, 0
                LONG    0, 0, 0, 0, 0
                LONG    0, 0, 0, 0, 0

DAT { tokens }

sNegTok         BYTE    "NEG", 0
sPosTok         BYTE    "POS", 0
sPlusTok        BYTE    "PLUS", 0
sMinusTok       BYTE    "MINUS", 0
sNaTok          BYTE    "NA", 0
sPassTok        BYTE    "PASS", 0
sFailTok        BYTE    "FAIL", 0
sMeasuredTok    BYTE    "MEASURED", 0
sProvisTok      BYTE    "PROVISIONAL", 0
sFixedTok       BYTE    "FIXED", 0
sSpeedTok       BYTE    "BY_SPEED", 0
sRevATok        BYTE    "REV_A", 0
sRevBTok        BYTE    "REV_B", 0
sUnknownTok     BYTE    "UNKNOWN", 0
sUserTok        BYTE    "USER", 0
sDocoTok        BYTE    "DOCO_BENCH", 0
sWheelTok       BYTE    "WHEEL_BENCH", 0
sNotRunTok      BYTE    "NOT_RUN", 0
sSkippedTok     BYTE    "SKIPPED", 0
sCleanTok       BYTE    "CLEAN", 0
sRoughTok       BYTE    "ROUGH", 0
sDroopTok       BYTE    "DROOP", 0
sHuntTok        BYTE    "HUNT", 0
sCappedTok      BYTE    "CAPPED", 0
sWallTok        BYTE    "WALL", 0
sFaultTok       BYTE    "FAULT", 0
sStoppedTok     BYTE    "STOPPED", 0
sStartTok       BYTE    "START", 0
sBoundTok       BYTE    "BOUND", 0
sLimitTok       BYTE    "LIMIT", 0
sBracketTok     BYTE    "BRACKETED", 0
sReserveTok     BYTE    "RESERVE", 0
sTopTok         BYTE    "TOP", 0
sNoneTok        BYTE    "NONE", 0
sNoRecordTok    BYTE    "NO_RECORD", 0
sRecFormatTok   BYTE    "RECORD_FORMAT", 0
sGeometryTok    BYTE    "GEOMETRY", 0
sRecPlanTok     BYTE    "RECORD_PLAN", 0
sConfigTok      BYTE    "CONFIG", 0
sBoardTok       BYTE    "BOARD", 0
sZeroTok        BYTE    "ZERO", 0
sOverTok        BYTE    "OVER_CURRENT", 0
sChargeTok      BYTE    "CHARGE_CAP", 0
sTimeTok        BYTE    "TIME_CAP", 0
sFaultStuckTok  BYTE    "FAULT_STUCK", 0
sStopTimeTok    BYTE    "STOP_TIMEOUT", 0
sRestoreTok     BYTE    "RESTORE", 0

VAR { the record, the run, the guards }

    LONG    rec[REC_LONGS]                                  ' the motor's record, copied from the table
    LONG    bRecordFound                                    ' T/F: a usable record was found
    LONG    eAbortReason                                    ' AR_*: why the run ended early (the first cause)
    LONG    abortDetail                                     ' its detail
    LONG    runStartMs                                      ' getms() at the start
    LONG    nRungs                                          ' the ladder's rung count, from the record
    LONG    estS                                            ' the run's estimated driven time, s
    LONG    abortMa                                         ' the absolute abort, mA
    LONG    wallCeilMa                                      ' the current wall's ceiling, mA
    LONG    chargeCapSamples                                ' the charge cap, mA x readings (one reading is SAMPLE_MS)
    LONG    timeCapMs                                       ' the time cap, ms
    LONG    chargeSamples                                   ' the charge so far, mA x readings
    LONG    peakMa                                          ' the highest DC link read, mA
    LONG    overSamples                                     ' readings in a row at or over the absolute abort

VAR { the motor as started }

    LONG    eBoard                                          ' REV_A, REV_B or REV_Unknown
    LONG    mvPerA                                          ' the current sense's scale for that board, mV per A
    LONG    zeroMvX10                                       ' the rest zero, mV x 10
    LONG    dutyMax                                         ' the drive's duty ceiling
    LONG    toldMv                                          ' the voltage it was started at, mV
    LONG    startFwd                                        ' the pair it started with: negative increments, degrees ...
    LONG    startRev                                        ' ... positive increments
    LONG    bStartBySpeed                                   ' T/F where T means the driver sets the pair by speed (the lead table)

VAR { the sampler and its window }

    LONG    smpPeriodCt, smpNextCt, smpCt, smpMs
    LONG    smpSenseMv, smpDuty, smpState, bSmpFault, smpHeld, smpCapped, smpDrvIncr, smpPos
    LONG    winN, winSenseSum, winDutySum, winPos0, winHeld0, winCap0, winCt0, winResync0
    LONG    winDcMa, winDuty, winFolPm, winHeldD, winCapD, winResyncD

VAR { the offset scan: the speed and sign under way, and each one's fit }

    LONG    ptD[OFS_POINTS]                                 ' a point's degrees from the start pair
    LONG    ptDeg[OFS_POINTS]                               ' the offset applied, degrees
    LONG    ptOutcome[OFS_POINTS]                           ' PO_*
    LONG    ptDcMa[OFS_POINTS]                              ' its DC link, mA
    LONG    ptDuty[OFS_POINTS]                              ' its mean duty
    LONG    ptFolPm[OFS_POINTS]                             ' its following, per mille
    LONG    ptHeld[OFS_POINTS]                              ' its held passes
    LONG    ptCapped[OFS_POINTS]                            ' its duty-capped passes
    LONG    ptResyncs[OFS_POINTS]                           ' its re-synced faults
    LONG    sideEnd[2]                                      ' each side's end: PO_* or END_LIMIT
    LONG    bFitOk[SPEEDS * SIGNS]                          ' T/F: the fit resolved
    LONG    fitAbsX10[SPEEDS * SIGNS]                       ' its minimum, absolute, tenths of a degree, -1_800 .. 1_800
    LONG    fitFromX10[SPEEDS * SIGNS]                      ' its minimum from the start pair, tenths
    LONG    fitSeX10[SPEEDS * SIGNS]                        ' the minimum's standard error, tenths
    LONG    fitPts[SPEEDS * SIGNS]                          ' the points fitted
    LONG    zX10[SPEEDS]                                    ' each speed's Z, tenths (when both signs resolved)
    LONG    leadX10[SPEEDS]                                 ' each speed's lead, tenths
    LONG    bPairOk[SPEEDS]                                 ' T/F: both signs resolved at the speed
    LONG    eZVerdict                                       ' VD_*
    LONG    bScanRan                                        ' T/F: the scan was entered

VAR { the ceiling ladder: the sign under way, and each sign's ceiling }

    LONG    rgIncr[RUNGS_MAX]                               ' a rung's increment, signed
    LONG    rgOutcome[RUNGS_MAX]                            ' PO_*
    LONG    rgDuty[RUNGS_MAX]                               ' its mean duty
    LONG    rgFolPm[RUNGS_MAX]                              ' its following
    LONG    rgDcMa[RUNGS_MAX]                               ' its DC link, mA
    LONG    rgHeld[RUNGS_MAX]                               ' its held passes
    LONG    rgCapped[RUNGS_MAX]                             ' its duty-capped passes
    LONG    ceilEnd[SIGNS]                                  ' how the climb ended: PO_* or END_*
    LONG    ceilIncr[SIGNS]                                 ' the sign's ceiling, increment magnitude (0: none)
    LONG    resIncr[SIGNS]                                  ' the duty line's reserve increment (0: no line)
    LONG    bResBracketed[SIGNS]                            ' T/F: the reserve lies at or below the fastest clean rung
    LONG    topCleanIncr[SIGNS]                             ' the fastest clean rung, increment magnitude
    LONG    cleanRungs[SIGNS]                               ' the clean rungs
    LONG    bCeilFound[SIGNS]                               ' T/F: the climb gave a ceiling (the CEILING check)
    LONG    bLadderRan                                      ' T/F: the ladder was entered

PUB main() | bGoOn
'' Adopt the configured motor: find its record, start it, scan its offsets, measure its ceiling, print the result.
''

' Local Variables:
' @local bGoOn - T/F where T means nothing so far has ended the run

    runStartMs := getms()
    eAbortReason := AR_NONE
    emitBanner()
    bGoOn := bSelectRecord()                                ' before anything is started: a motor with no record is refused
    if bGoOn
        bGoOn := bPlanRun()
    if bGoOn
        bGoOn := bStartMotor()
    if bGoOn
        bGoOn := bMeasureZero()
    if bGoOn
        bGoOn := bRunScan()
    if bGoOn
        bGoOn := bRunLadder()
    shutdown()                                              ' the motor stops on every way out
    emitResult()
    emitEnd()
#ifdef BENCH_CFG
    debug("DEBUG_END_SESSION")                              ' our bench's runner closes its terminal on this line
#endif

CON { --- the record, the plan, the start --- }

PRI bSelectRecord() : bFound | idx, nKey, bEnded, nTicksLib
' Find the record keyed by the configured MOTOR_TYPE and copy it; refuse (MA-REFUSE) a motor type with no record, a
' record of another layout, or one whose hall ticks per revolution are not the driver's. Emits MA-RECORD. Nothing is
' started.
'
' @returns bFound - T/F where T means the record is found and usable

' Local Variables:
' @local idx - a record in the table
' @local nKey - its key
' @local bEnded - T/F where T means the walk has found the record or the table's end
' @local nTicksLib - the driver's hall ticks per revolution for the configured motor

    bFound := FALSE
    bEnded := FALSE
    longfill(@rec, 0, REC_LONGS)
    repeat idx from 0 to RECORDS_MAX - 1
        if bEnded == FALSE
            nKey := motorRecords[idx * REC_LONGS + REC_KEY]
            if nKey == END_OF_RECORDS
                bEnded := TRUE
            elseif nKey == user.MOTOR_TYPE
                longmove(@rec, @motorRecords[idx * REC_LONGS], REC_LONGS)
                bFound := TRUE
                bEnded := TRUE
    _, nTicksLib := wheel.hallTicInfoForMotor()
    emitRecord(bFound)
    if bFound == FALSE
        refuse(AR_NO_RECORD, user.MOTOR_TYPE)
    elseif rec[REC_FORMAT] <> RECORD_FORMAT
        bFound := FALSE
        refuse(AR_RECORD_FORMAT, rec[REC_FORMAT])
    elseif rec[REC_TICKS_PER_REV] <> nTicksLib
        bFound := FALSE
        refuse(AR_GEOMETRY, nTicksLib)
    bRecordFound := bFound

PRI bPlanRun() : bPlanned | nScanS, nLadderS
' Check the record's plan can run (two scan speeds and every rung under the field-step margin, a ladder of 2 to
' RUNGS_MAX rungs) and the configuration is legal; then derive the run's estimate and its guards from the record.
' Emits MA-PLAN. Nothing is started.
'
' @returns bPlanned - T/F where T means the plan and the configuration are usable

' Local Variables:
' @local nScanS - the offset scan's estimated driven time at most, s
' @local nLadderS - the ladder's, s

    bPlanned := FALSE
    nRungs := 0
    if rec[REC_LADDER_STEP_RPM] > 0
        nRungs := (rec[REC_LADDER_TO_RPM] - rec[REC_LADDER_FROM_RPM]) / rec[REC_LADDER_STEP_RPM] + 1
    if (rec[REC_SLOW_RPM] < 1) or (rec[REC_FAST_RPM] <= rec[REC_SLOW_RPM]) or (incrForRpm(rec[REC_FAST_RPM]) > PK1_CAP_INCR)
        refuse(AR_RECORD_PLAN, rec[REC_FAST_RPM])
    elseif (nRungs < 2) or (nRungs > RUNGS_MAX) or (rec[REC_LADDER_FROM_RPM] < 1)
        refuse(AR_RECORD_PLAN, nRungs)
    elseif (rec[REC_RATED_MA] < 1) or (rec[REC_SCAN_A] < 1) or (rec[REC_LADDER_A] < 1)
        refuse(AR_RECORD_PLAN, rec[REC_RATED_MA])
    elseif wheel.validBasePinForChoice(MOTOR_BASE) == wheel.INVALID_PIN_BASE
        refuse(AR_CONFIG, MOTOR_BASE)
    elseif wheel.validVoltageForChoice(user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE) == wheel.INVALID_VOLTAGE
        refuse(AR_CONFIG, user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE)
    elseif wheel.validMotorForChoice(user.MOTOR_TYPE) == wheel.INVALID_MOTOR
        refuse(AR_CONFIG, user.MOTOR_TYPE)
    elseif wheel.validDetectModeForChoice(MOTOR_BOARD_TYPE) == wheel.INVALID_DET_MODE
        refuse(AR_CONFIG, MOTOR_BOARD_TYPE)
    else
        bPlanned := TRUE
    ' at most: every side walked to its 90 degrees, every rung climbed
    nScanS := SPEEDS * SIGNS * 2 * (OFS_SIDE_POINTS * (SETTLE_MS + WINDOW_MS) / wheel.MS_PER_SEC + 2 * EST_CHANGE_S)
    nLadderS := SIGNS * ((nRungs #> 0) * ((SETTLE_MS + WINDOW_MS) / wheel.MS_PER_SEC + EST_STEP_S) + 2 * EST_CHANGE_S)
    estS := nScanS + nLadderS
    abortMa := ABORT_X_RATED * rec[REC_RATED_MA]
    wallCeilMa := abortMa * WALL_CEIL_PCT / X100
    chargeCapSamples := (rec[REC_RATED_MA] * CHARGE_RATED_S + rec[REC_NO_LOAD_MA] * estS) * SAMPLES_PER_SEC
    timeCapMs := TIME_FACTOR * estS * wheel.MS_PER_SEC
    benchLog.begin(@"MA-PLAN")
    benchLog.numField(@"est_s", estS, LIM_MID)
    benchLog.numField(@"time_cap_s", timeCapMs / wheel.MS_PER_SEC, LIM_MID)
    benchLog.numField(@"charge_cap_mas", chargeCapSamples / SAMPLES_PER_SEC, LIM_BIG)
    benchLog.numField(@"abort_ma", abortMa, LIM_MID)
    benchLog.numField(@"wall_ceil_ma", wallCeilMa, LIM_MID)
    benchLog.numField(@"rungs", nRungs, LIM_TINY)
    benchLog.numField(@"step_deg", OFS_STEP_DEG, LIM_TINY)
    benchLog.numField(@"max_deg", OFS_SIDE_STEPS * OFS_STEP_DEG, LIM_TINY)
    benchLog.numField(@"cap_incr", PK1_CAP_INCR, LIM_BIG)
    benchLog.boolField(@"ok", bPlanned)
    lineEmit()

PRI bStartMotor() : bStarted | motorCog, eStartErr, nWaitStart, bReady, ePack, nPackMv
' Start the motor with its start checks refusing, coasting at rest; wait until it is ready; read the board it detected,
' the drive's duty ceiling, the voltage it was told and the commutation it starts with; put it under the scan's test
' current limit. Emits MA-START (and MA-LIMIT). Nothing moves but the start checks' pulses.
'
' @returns bStarted - T/F where T means the motor is ready, its board known and its test limit in force

' Local Variables:
' @local motorCog - start()'s result: the driver's cog, or -1
' @local eStartErr - getError() after a refused start, else NO_ERROR
' @local nWaitStart - getms() when the ready wait began
' @local bReady - T/F where T means isReady() came true in time
' @local ePack - the pack sensor's status
' @local nPackMv - its reading, mV

    bStarted := FALSE
    eStartErr := wheel.NO_ERROR
    bReady := FALSE
    wheel.setStartChecks(TRUE)
    wheel.holdAtStop(FALSE)
    benchLog.cogEventBegin()
    motorCog := wheel.start(MOTOR_BASE, user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE, MOTOR_BOARD_TYPE)
    benchLog.cogEventEnd()
    if motorCog < 0
        eStartErr := wheel.getError()
    else
        nWaitStart := getms()
        repeat until wheel.isReady() or (getms() - nWaitStart >= READY_TIMEOUT_MS)
            waitms(READY_POLL_MS)
        bReady := wheel.isReady()
    eBoard := wheel.getBoardType()
    mvPerA := wheel.F_REV_B_RSENSE
    if eBoard == wheel.REV_A
        mvPerA := wheel.F_REV_A_RSENSE
    _, _, _, dutyMax, _, _ := wheel.testGetDriveConstants()
    _, toldMv := wheel.getDriveVoltage()
    ePack, nPackMv := wheel.getPackVoltage()
    startFwd, startRev := wheel.testGetFwdRevIndep()
    bStartBySpeed, _ := wheel.testGetLead()
    benchLog.begin(@"MA-START")
    benchLog.numField(@"cog", motorCog, LIM_TINY)
    benchLog.numField(@"err", eStartErr, LIM_SMALL)
    benchLog.boolField(@"ready", bReady)
    benchLog.tokenField(@"board", boardToken(eBoard), TOKMAX)
    benchLog.numField(@"mv_per_a", mvPerA, LIM_SMALL)
    benchLog.numField(@"told_mv", toldMv, LIM_MID)
    benchLog.naNumField(@"pack_mv", nPackMv, LIM_MID, ePack == wheel.PACK_PRESENT)
    benchLog.numField(@"fwd_deg", startFwd, LIM_SMALL)
    benchLog.numField(@"rev_deg", startRev, LIM_SMALL)
    benchLog.tokenField(@"lead", leadToken(bStartBySpeed), TOKMAX)
    benchLog.numField(@"duty_max", dutyMax, LIM_MID)
    benchLog.numField(@"clk_hz", clkfreq, LIM_BIG)
    lineEmit()
    if (motorCog < 0) or (bReady == FALSE)
        setAbort(AR_START, eStartErr)
    elseif eBoard == wheel.REV_Unknown
        setAbort(AR_BOARD, eBoard)
    else
        bStarted := bSetLimit(rec[REC_SCAN_A])

PRI bSetLimit(nAmps) : bSet | eLimErr, nPeakA, nContA
' Put the motor under a test current limit of {nAmps}, peak and continuous, and read it back (at rest). Emits MA-LIMIT.
' A limit not taken ends the run before anything moves.
'
' @param nAmps - the limit, whole amps
' @returns bSet - T/F where T means it reads back as asked

' Local Variables:
' @local eLimErr - testSetCurrentLimits()'s result
' @local nPeakA - the peak limit read back, A
' @local nContA - the continuous limit read back, A

    eLimErr := wheel.testSetCurrentLimits(nAmps, nAmps)
    nPeakA, nContA, _, _, _ := wheel.testGetCurrentLimitState()
    bSet := (eLimErr == wheel.NO_ERROR) and (nPeakA == nAmps) and (nContA == nAmps)
    benchLog.begin(@"MA-LIMIT")
    benchLog.numField(@"amps", nAmps, LIM_TINY)
    benchLog.numField(@"err", eLimErr, LIM_SMALL)
    benchLog.numField(@"peak_a", nPeakA, LIM_TINY)
    benchLog.numField(@"cont_a", nContA, LIM_TINY)
    benchLog.boolField(@"set", bSet)
    lineEmit()
    if bSet == FALSE
        setAbort(AR_LIMIT, nPeakA)

PRI bMeasureZero() : bHealthy | nSample, nSumMv, nMinMv, nMaxMv, nSenseMv, nLoMv, nHiMv
' Read the current sense's rest zero with the bridge coasting: ZERO_SAMPLES readings SAMPLE_MS apart. It must be alive
' (its readings differ) and inside the driver's own band for the board it detected, or no current guard could work.
' Emits MA-ZERO.
'
' @returns bHealthy - T/F where T means the zero is alive and in its band

' Local Variables:
' @local nSample - the reading being taken
' @local nSumMv - the readings' sum, mV
' @local nMinMv - the lowest, mV
' @local nMaxMv - the highest, mV
' @local nSenseMv - one reading, mV
' @local nLoMv - the band's low end, mV
' @local nHiMv - its high end, mV

    nSumMv := 0
    nMinMv := posx
    nMaxMv := negx
    repeat nSample from 1 to ZERO_SAMPLES
        _, _, nSenseMv, _, _, _, _, _ := wheel.testGetTelemetry()
        nSumMv += nSenseMv
        nMinMv <#= nSenseMv
        nMaxMv #>= nSenseMv
        waitms(SAMPLE_MS)
    zeroMvX10 := divRound(nSumMv * X10, ZERO_SAMPLES)
    nLoMv := wheel.REST_ZERO_MIN_MV
    nHiMv := wheel.REST_ZERO_MAX_MV
    if eBoard == wheel.REV_A
        nLoMv := wheel.REST_ZERO_MIN_MV_REVA
        nHiMv := wheel.REST_ZERO_MAX_MV_REVA
    bHealthy := (nMaxMv - nMinMv >= ZERO_SPREAD_MIN_MV) and (zeroMvX10 >= nLoMv * X10) and (zeroMvX10 <= nHiMv * X10)
    benchLog.begin(@"MA-ZERO")
    benchLog.numField(@"zero_mv_x10", zeroMvX10, LIM_MID)
    benchLog.numField(@"spread_mv", nMaxMv - nMinMv, LIM_SMALL)
    benchLog.numField(@"band_lo_mv", nLoMv, LIM_SMALL)
    benchLog.numField(@"band_hi_mv", nHiMv, LIM_SMALL)
    benchLog.boolField(@"healthy", bHealthy)
    lineEmit()
    if bHealthy == FALSE
        setAbort(AR_ZERO, zeroMvX10)

PRI shutdown()
' Stop the motor: safe whether or not it started, and on every way out.

    benchLog.cogEventBegin()
    wheel.stop()

CON { --- the offset scan --- }

PRI bRunScan() : bGoOn | eSpeed, eSign, bRestored
' The offset scan: at each scan speed, negative then positive increments (bScanSpeedSign()); then the commutation the
' driver started with put back, whatever ended the scan; then each speed's pair and the Z check.
'
' @returns bGoOn - T/F where T means nothing ended the run and the commutation is back as it started

' Local Variables:
' @local eSpeed - SPEED_SLOW or SPEED_FAST
' @local eSign - SIGN_NEG or SIGN_POS
' @local bRestored - T/F where T means the starting commutation is back

    bGoOn := TRUE
    bScanRan := TRUE
    repeat eSpeed from SPEED_SLOW to SPEED_FAST
        repeat eSign from SIGN_NEG to SIGN_POS
            bFitOk[eSpeed * SIGNS + eSign] := FALSE
            if bGoOn
                bGoOn := bScanSpeedSign(eSpeed, eSign)
    bRestored := bRestoreCommutation()
    bGoOn := bGoOn and bRestored
    pairsAndZ()

PRI bScanSpeedSign(eSpeed, eSign) : bGoOn | nIncr, slotIdx, eSide, spIdx
' One speed and one increment sign: both sides of the start pair (bScanSide()), then at rest every point's record, the
' fit (fitScan()) and MA-FIT.
'
' @param eSpeed - SPEED_SLOW or SPEED_FAST
' @param eSign - SIGN_NEG or SIGN_POS
' @returns bGoOn - T/F where T means nothing ended the run

' Local Variables:
' @local nIncr - the speed's increment, signed
' @local slotIdx - a point's slot
' @local eSide - SIDE_PLUS or SIDE_MINUS
' @local spIdx - the speed and sign's fit slot

    bGoOn := TRUE
    spIdx := eSpeed * SIGNS + eSign
    nIncr := incrForRpm(rec[REC_SLOW_RPM + eSpeed])
    if eSign == SIGN_NEG
        nIncr := -nIncr
    repeat slotIdx from 0 to OFS_POINTS - 1
        ptOutcome[slotIdx] := PO_NOT_RUN
        ptD[slotIdx] := 0
        ptDeg[slotIdx] := 0
    repeat eSide from SIDE_PLUS to SIDE_MINUS
        sideEnd[eSide] := PO_NOT_RUN
        if bGoOn
            bGoOn := bScanSide(eSign, eSide, nIncr)
    repeat slotIdx from 0 to OFS_POINTS - 1
        if ptOutcome[slotIdx] <> PO_NOT_RUN
            emitPoint(eSpeed, eSign, slotIdx)
    repeat eSide from SIDE_PLUS to SIDE_MINUS
        emitSide(eSpeed, eSign, eSide)
    fitScan(spIdx)
    emitFit(eSpeed, eSign, spIdx)

PRI bScanSide(eSign, eSide, nIncr) : bGoOn | eUp, stepIdx, slotIdx, nD, nLimitMa, nRefMa, nPrevMa, bSeenClean, bEnded, bResting, nEdgeRun, ePo, nLowCleanD, nLowCleanMa
' One side of the start pair at one speed: at rest the start pair, from rest to the speed, then each point outward (the
' start pair first), the offset changed while driven by one step; a WALL or a FAULT ends the side at once, EDGE_RUN
' DROOP or HUNT points in a row end it, and its 90 degrees end it. PL-209 (TOOL_REV 4): so does a point FIT_HALF_DEG
' past the side's lowest CLEAN point (END_BRACKETED) -- the fit uses no point further out, and at the library's 40 A
' nothing caps the current where the motor's torque collapses (D2: every Doco run ended on 4.5-10.2 A about 30 degrees
' past a minimum it had already bracketed). A side still falling walks on, since its lowest point moves with it. Until the side has seen a CLEAN point, a DROOP or
' HUNT point drawing less current than the point before it does not count toward the run (it restarts it): the walk is
' still coming down toward a minimum it has not reached, as it must when a driver's start pair sits in the hunting
' region. The current wall's relative threshold follows the lowest CLEAN or ROUGH point so far (until the first, only the
' wall's ceiling applies, as the 6.5in scan did). Then stopped and, at rest, the start pair again.
'
' @param eSign - SIGN_NEG or SIGN_POS
' @param eSide - SIDE_PLUS or SIDE_MINUS
' @param nIncr - the speed's increment, signed
' @returns bGoOn - T/F where T means nothing ended the run

' Local Variables:
' @local eUp - the way up's outcome, RO_*
' @local stepIdx - the point within the side, 0 = the start pair
' @local slotIdx - its slot
' @local nD - its degrees from the start pair
' @local nLimitMa - the current wall's relative threshold, mA (0, none, until a reference is measured)
' @local nRefMa - the lowest CLEAN or ROUGH point's DC link so far, mA (posx until one)
' @local nPrevMa - the previous point's DC link, mA
' @local bSeenClean - T/F where T means the side has measured a CLEAN point
' @local bEnded - T/F where T means the side has ended
' @local bResting - T/F where T means the motor already rests (a refusal or a fault's recovery left it there)
' @local nEdgeRun - DROOP or HUNT points in a row that count
' @local ePo - a point's outcome
' @local nLowCleanD - the lowest CLEAN point's degrees from the start pair (PL-209)
' @local nLowCleanMa - its DC link, mA (posx until one)

    bGoOn := TRUE
    bEnded := FALSE
    bResting := FALSE
    bSeenClean := FALSE
    nLowCleanD := 0
    nLowCleanMa := posx
    nEdgeRun := 0
    nLimitMa := 0
    nRefMa := posx
    nPrevMa := 0
    applyOffset(eSign, 0)
    sampleBegin()
    eUp := driveTo(nIncr)
    if eUp == RO_REFUSED
        sideEnd[eSide] := PO_START
        bEnded := TRUE
        bResting := TRUE
    elseif eUp == RO_FAULT
        sideEnd[eSide] := PO_START
        bEnded := TRUE
        bResting := TRUE
        bGoOn := bFaultRecover()
    elseif eUp == RO_STOPPED
        bGoOn := FALSE
    repeat stepIdx from 0 to OFS_SIDE_STEPS
        slotIdx := eSide * OFS_SIDE_POINTS + stepIdx
        nD := stepIdx * OFS_STEP_DEG
        if eSide == SIDE_MINUS
            nD := -nD
        ptD[slotIdx] := nD
        if bGoOn and (bEnded == FALSE)
            ptDeg[slotIdx] := applyOffset(eSign, nD)
            ePo := measurePoint(slotIdx, nIncr, nLimitMa)
            ptOutcome[slotIdx] := ePo
            if (ePo == PO_DROOP) or (ePo == PO_HUNT)
                if bSeenClean or (stepIdx == 0) or (ptDcMa[slotIdx] >= nPrevMa)
                    nEdgeRun++
                else
                    nEdgeRun := 0                           ' still coming down toward a minimum not yet reached
            else
                nEdgeRun := 0
            if ePo == PO_CLEAN
                bSeenClean := TRUE
                if ptDcMa[slotIdx] < nLowCleanMa                ' PL-209: the side's lowest clean point so far
                    nLowCleanMa := ptDcMa[slotIdx]
                    nLowCleanD := nD
            if (ePo == PO_CLEAN) or (ePo == PO_ROUGH)
                nRefMa <#= ptDcMa[slotIdx]
                nLimitMa := ((nRefMa #> 0) * WALL_REL_X100 / X100 #> rec[REC_NO_LOAD_MA]) <# wallCeilMa
            nPrevMa := ptDcMa[slotIdx]
            if (ePo == PO_WALL) or (nEdgeRun >= EDGE_RUN)
                sideEnd[eSide] := ePo
                bEnded := TRUE
            elseif ePo == PO_FAULT
                sideEnd[eSide] := ePo
                bEnded := TRUE
                bResting := TRUE
                bGoOn := bFaultRecover()
            elseif ePo == PO_STOPPED
                bGoOn := FALSE
            elseif bSeenClean and (abs(nD - nLowCleanD) >= FIT_HALF_DEG)
                sideEnd[eSide] := END_BRACKETED                 ' PL-209: the fit has every point it can use
                bEnded := TRUE
        elseif bGoOn
            ptOutcome[slotIdx] := PO_SKIPPED
    if bGoOn and (bEnded == FALSE)
        sideEnd[eSide] := END_LIMIT
    if bGoOn and (bResting == FALSE)
        bGoOn := bStopAndRest()
    applyOffset(eSign, 0)

PRI measurePoint(slotIdx, nIncr, nLimitMa) : ePo | eRo, nNetMa, nOver, nCeil, nStartMs, eOutcome
' One point, its offset just applied: SETTLE_MS, then a WINDOW_MS window with the current wall watched at each reading;
' then the point's readings kept and its outcome classified (classify()).
'
' @param slotIdx - the point's slot
' @param nIncr - the speed's increment, signed
' @param nLimitMa - the current wall's relative threshold, mA (0: none yet, the wall's ceiling only)
' @returns ePo - PO_CLEAN, PO_ROUGH, PO_DROOP, PO_HUNT, PO_WALL, PO_FAULT or PO_STOPPED

' Local Variables:
' @local eRo - the settle's outcome
' @local nNetMa - a reading's DC link, mA
' @local nOver - readings in a row over the relative threshold
' @local nCeil - readings in a row over the wall's ceiling
' @local nStartMs - the window's start, getms()
' @local eOutcome - a reading's outcome

    ePo := PO_CLEAN
    nOver := 0
    nCeil := 0
    windowClear()
    eRo := waitPhase(UNTIL_ELAPSED, 0, SETTLE_MS)
    if eRo == RO_FAULT
        ePo := PO_FAULT
    elseif eRo == RO_STOPPED
        ePo := PO_STOPPED
    else
        windowBegin()
        nStartMs := smpMs
        repeat
            eOutcome := sampleNext()
            windowAdd()
            if eOutcome == GO_FAULT
                ePo := PO_FAULT
                quit
            if bGuardStops(eOutcome)
                ePo := PO_STOPPED
                quit
            nNetMa := netMilliamps(smpSenseMv)
            nCeil := (nNetMa >= wallCeilMa) ? nCeil + 1 : 0
            nOver := ((nLimitMa > 0) and (nNetMa > nLimitMa)) ? nOver + 1 : 0
            if (nCeil >= ABS_ABORT_SAMPLES) or (nOver >= WALL_REL_SAMPLES)
                ePo := PO_WALL
                quit
            if smpMs - nStartMs >= WINDOW_MS
                quit
        windowEnd(nIncr)
    ptDcMa[slotIdx] := winDcMa
    ptDuty[slotIdx] := winDuty
    ptFolPm[slotIdx] := winFolPm
    ptHeld[slotIdx] := winHeldD
    ptCapped[slotIdx] := winCapD
    ptResyncs[slotIdx] := winResyncD
    if ePo == PO_CLEAN
        ePo := classify(FALSE)

PRI classify(bLadder) : ePo
' A window that finished: DROOP under DROOP_PM of the command; HUNT with HUNT_HELD_MIN held passes; on the ladder,
' CAPPED with a duty-capped pass; CLEAN following within FOLLOW_TOL_PM with no re-sync; else ROUGH.
'
' @param bLadder - T/F where T means a ladder rung (a capped pass is an edge there)
' @returns ePo - PO_DROOP, PO_HUNT, PO_CAPPED, PO_CLEAN or PO_ROUGH

    if winFolPm < DROOP_PM
        ePo := PO_DROOP
    elseif winHeldD >= HUNT_HELD_MIN
        ePo := PO_HUNT
    elseif bLadder and (winCapD > 0)
        ePo := PO_CAPPED
    elseif (abs(winFolPm - PM) <= FOLLOW_TOL_PM) and (winResyncD == 0) and (winCapD == 0)
        ePo := PO_CLEAN
    else
        ePo := PO_ROUGH

PRI applyOffset(eSign, nD) : nApplied | nFwd, nRev
' Set the offset {eSign} uses to the start pair's plus {nD} degrees, the other sign's left at the start pair (the driver
' applies its NEG offset to negative increments and its POS offset to positive ones), and read back what it applies.
'
' @param eSign - SIGN_NEG or SIGN_POS
' @param nD - degrees from the start pair
' @returns nApplied - the offset that sign now uses, degrees (0..359)

' Local Variables:
' @local nFwd - the pair read back: negative increments
' @local nRev - positive increments

    if eSign == SIGN_NEG
        wheel.testSetFwdRevIndep(startFwd + nD, startRev)
    else
        wheel.testSetFwdRevIndep(startFwd, startRev + nD)
    nFwd, nRev := wheel.testGetFwdRevIndep()
    nApplied := nRev
    if eSign == SIGN_NEG
        nApplied := nFwd

PRI bRestoreCommutation() : bRestored | nFwd, nRev
' Put back the commutation the driver started with: the start pair, and the speed-set lead where the driver uses one;
' read the pair back. A fixed pair that does not read back ends the run (the ceiling must be measured on it). Emits
' MA-RESTORE.
'
' @returns bRestored - T/F where T means the starting commutation is back

' Local Variables:
' @local nFwd - the pair read back: negative increments
' @local nRev - positive increments

    wheel.testSetFwdRevIndep(startFwd, startRev)
    nFwd, nRev := wheel.testGetFwdRevIndep()
    bRestored := (nFwd == startFwd) and (nRev == startRev)
    if bStartBySpeed
        bRestored := bRestored and (wheel.testSetLeadScheduled(TRUE) == wheel.NO_ERROR)
    benchLog.begin(@"MA-RESTORE")
    benchLog.numField(@"fwd_deg", nFwd, LIM_SMALL)
    benchLog.numField(@"rev_deg", nRev, LIM_SMALL)
    benchLog.tokenField(@"lead", leadToken(bStartBySpeed), TOKMAX)
    benchLog.boolField(@"restored", bRestored)
    lineEmit()
    if bRestored == FALSE
        setAbort(AR_RESTORE, nFwd)

PRI fitScan(spIdx) | slotIdx, nLowD, nLowMa, nLoD, nHiD, nPts, fU, fY, fS0, fS1, fS2, fS3, fS4, fT0, fT1, fT2, fDet, fA, fB, fC, fSsr, fResVar, fCaa, fCbb, fCab, fVert, fVse, nVertX10, nVseX10
' The current minimum of one speed and sign: the parabola y = a u^2 + b u + c, u = degrees from the start pair / 10, y the
' DC link, by least squares over the clean points within FIT_HALF_DEG of the lowest clean one; its vertex -b / 2a, and
' the vertex's standard error by the delta method through the inverse normal matrix. RESOLVED with FIT_MIN_PTS points,
' a above 0, the vertex inside the points fitted, and its standard error at most VERT_SE_MAX_X10.
'
' @param spIdx - the speed and sign's fit slot

' Local Variables:
' @local slotIdx - a point's slot
' @local nLowD - the lowest clean point's degrees from the start pair
' @local nLowMa - its DC link, mA
' @local nLoD - the fitted points' smallest degrees
' @local nHiD - their largest
' @local nPts - the points fitted
' @local fU - a point's u
' @local fY - its DC link
' @local fS0 - float sum of u^0
' @local fS1 - sum of u
' @local fS2 - sum of u^2
' @local fS3 - sum of u^3
' @local fS4 - sum of u^4
' @local fT0 - sum of y
' @local fT1 - sum of y u
' @local fT2 - sum of y u^2
' @local fDet - the normal matrix's determinant
' @local fA - the curvature
' @local fB - the slope at the start pair
' @local fC - the level there
' @local fSsr - the sum of squared residuals
' @local fResVar - the residual variance
' @local fCaa - the inverse matrix's (a, a) element
' @local fCbb - its (b, b) element
' @local fCab - its (a, b) element
' @local fVert - the vertex, u
' @local fVse - its variance, u^2
' @local nVertX10 - the vertex, tenths of a degree from the start pair
' @local nVseX10 - its standard error, tenths

    bFitOk[spIdx] := FALSE
    fitFromX10[spIdx] := 0
    fitAbsX10[spIdx] := 0
    fitSeX10[spIdx] := LIM_SMALL
    nLowMa := posx
    nLowD := 0
    repeat slotIdx from 0 to OFS_POINTS - 1
        if (ptOutcome[slotIdx] == PO_CLEAN) and (ptDcMa[slotIdx] < nLowMa)
            nLowMa := ptDcMa[slotIdx]
            nLowD := ptD[slotIdx]
    nPts := 0
    nLoD := posx
    nHiD := negx
    fS0 := fS1 := fS2 := fS3 := fS4 := fT0 := fT1 := fT2 := 0.0
    repeat slotIdx from 0 to OFS_POINTS - 1
        if (ptOutcome[slotIdx] == PO_CLEAN) and (abs(ptD[slotIdx] - nLowD) <= FIT_HALF_DEG)
            nPts++
            nLoD <#= ptD[slotIdx]
            nHiD #>= ptD[slotIdx]
            fU := float(ptD[slotIdx]) /. 10.0
            fY := float(ptDcMa[slotIdx])
            fS0 := fS0 +. 1.0
            fS1 := fS1 +. fU
            fS2 := fS2 +. fU *. fU
            fS3 := fS3 +. fU *. fU *. fU
            fS4 := fS4 +. fU *. fU *. fU *. fU
            fT0 := fT0 +. fY
            fT1 := fT1 +. fY *. fU
            fT2 := fT2 +. fY *. fU *. fU
    fitPts[spIdx] := nPts
    if nPts >= FIT_MIN_PTS
        fDet := fS4 *. (fS2 *. fS0 -. fS1 *. fS1) -. fS3 *. (fS3 *. fS0 -. fS1 *. fS2) +. fS2 *. (fS3 *. fS1 -. fS2 *. fS2)
        if fabs(fDet) >. 0.000001
            fA := (fT2 *. (fS2 *. fS0 -. fS1 *. fS1) -. fS3 *. (fT1 *. fS0 -. fS1 *. fT0) +. fS2 *. (fT1 *. fS1 -. fS2 *. fT0)) /. fDet
            fB := (fS4 *. (fT1 *. fS0 -. fT0 *. fS1) -. fT2 *. (fS3 *. fS0 -. fS1 *. fS2) +. fS2 *. (fS3 *. fT0 -. fT1 *. fS2)) /. fDet
            fC := (fS4 *. (fS2 *. fT0 -. fS1 *. fT1) -. fS3 *. (fS3 *. fT0 -. fT1 *. fS2) +. fT2 *. (fS3 *. fS1 -. fS2 *. fS2)) /. fDet
            fSsr := 0.0
            repeat slotIdx from 0 to OFS_POINTS - 1
                if (ptOutcome[slotIdx] == PO_CLEAN) and (abs(ptD[slotIdx] - nLowD) <= FIT_HALF_DEG)
                    fU := float(ptD[slotIdx]) /. 10.0
                    fY := float(ptDcMa[slotIdx]) -. (fA *. fU *. fU +. fB *. fU +. fC)
                    fSsr := fSsr +. fY *. fY
            fResVar := fSsr /. float(nPts - 3)
            fCaa := (fS2 *. fS0 -. fS1 *. fS1) /. fDet
            fCbb := (fS4 *. fS0 -. fS2 *. fS2) /. fDet
            fCab := -.(fS3 *. fS0 -. fS1 *. fS2) /. fDet
            if fA >. 0.0
                fVert := -.fB /. (2.0 *. fA)
                nVertX10 := clampedRound(fVert *. 100.0, LIM_SMALL)
                ' the delta method through v = -b / 2a: dv/db = -1 / 2a, dv/da = b / 2a^2
                fVse := fResVar /. (4.0 *. fA *. fA) *. (fCbb +. (fB /. fA) *. (fB /. fA) *. fCaa -. 2.0 *. (fB /. fA) *. fCab)
                if fVse <. 0.0
                    fVse := 0.0
                nVseX10 := clampedRound(fsqrt(fVse) *. 100.0, LIM_SMALL)
                fitFromX10[spIdx] := nVertX10
                fitSeX10[spIdx] := nVseX10
                bFitOk[spIdx] := (nVseX10 <= VERT_SE_MAX_X10) and (nVertX10 >= nLoD * X10) and (nVertX10 <= nHiD * X10)
    fitAbsX10[spIdx] := wrapSigned(startOffset(spIdx // SIGNS) * X10 + fitFromX10[spIdx], TENTHS_PER_TURN)

PRI startOffset(eSign) : nDeg
' The start pair's offset for {eSign}, degrees.
'
' @param eSign - SIGN_NEG or SIGN_POS
' @returns nDeg - startFwd for SIGN_NEG, else startRev

    nDeg := startRev
    if eSign == SIGN_NEG
        nDeg := startFwd

PRI pairsAndZ() | eSpeed, spNeg, spPos, nDiff
' At the scan's end: per speed, MA-PAIR -- each direction's minimum, half their difference (the lead, L) and their
' midpoint (the hall zero, Z), when both resolved, taken round the circle so a pair either side of 0 or 180 degrees
' cannot alias; then the Z check across the two speeds (MA-ZCHECK).

' Local Variables:
' @local eSpeed - a speed
' @local spNeg - its NEG fit slot
' @local spPos - its POS fit slot
' @local nDiff - Z at the fast speed less Z at the slow, tenths

    repeat eSpeed from SPEED_SLOW to SPEED_FAST
        spNeg := eSpeed * SIGNS + SIGN_NEG
        spPos := eSpeed * SIGNS + SIGN_POS
        bPairOk[eSpeed] := bFitOk[spNeg] and bFitOk[spPos]
        leadX10[eSpeed] := wrapSigned(fitAbsX10[spNeg] - fitAbsX10[spPos], TENTHS_PER_TURN) / 2
        zX10[eSpeed] := wrapSigned(fitAbsX10[spPos] + leadX10[eSpeed], TENTHS_PER_TURN)
        benchLog.begin(@"MA-PAIR")
        benchLog.numField(@"rpm", rec[REC_SLOW_RPM + eSpeed], LIM_MID)
        benchLog.boolField(@"resolved", bPairOk[eSpeed])
        benchLog.naNumField(@"fwd_deg", degreesOf(fitAbsX10[spNeg]), LIM_SMALL, bFitOk[spNeg])
        benchLog.naNumField(@"rev_deg", degreesOf(fitAbsX10[spPos]), LIM_SMALL, bFitOk[spPos])
        benchLog.naNumField(@"fwd_x10", fitAbsX10[spNeg], LIM_SMALL, bFitOk[spNeg])
        benchLog.naNumField(@"rev_x10", fitAbsX10[spPos], LIM_SMALL, bFitOk[spPos])
        benchLog.naNumField(@"z_x10", zX10[eSpeed], LIM_SMALL, bPairOk[eSpeed])
        benchLog.naNumField(@"lead_x10", leadX10[eSpeed], LIM_SMALL, bPairOk[eSpeed])
        lineEmit()
    eZVerdict := VD_NA
    nDiff := 0
    if bPairOk[SPEED_SLOW] and bPairOk[SPEED_FAST]
        nDiff := wrapSigned(zX10[SPEED_FAST] - zX10[SPEED_SLOW], TENTHS_PER_TURN)
        eZVerdict := VD_FAIL
        if abs(nDiff) <= Z_AGREE_TOL_X10
            eZVerdict := VD_PASS
    benchLog.begin(@"MA-ZCHECK")
    benchLog.tokenField(@"verdict", verdictToken(eZVerdict), TOKMAX)
    benchLog.naNumField(@"z_slow_x10", zX10[SPEED_SLOW], LIM_SMALL, bPairOk[SPEED_SLOW])
    benchLog.naNumField(@"z_fast_x10", zX10[SPEED_FAST], LIM_SMALL, bPairOk[SPEED_FAST])
    benchLog.naNumField(@"diff_x10", nDiff, LIM_SMALL, eZVerdict <> VD_NA)
    benchLog.numField(@"tol_x10", Z_AGREE_TOL_X10, LIM_SMALL)
    lineEmit()

PRI degreesOf(nTenths) : nDeg
' A signed angle in tenths of a degree as whole degrees 0..359, rounded: the form offsetsForMotor() returns.
'
' @param nTenths - the angle, tenths of a degree, either sign
' @returns nDeg - whole degrees, 0..359

    nDeg := wrapPositive(divRound(nTenths, X10), TENTHS_PER_TURN / X10)

CON { --- the ceiling ladder --- }

PRI bRunLadder() : bGoOn | eSign
' The ceiling: under the record's ladder test limit, each sign NEG then POS, a climb (bClimb()) on the commutation the
' driver started with; then the scan's limit again.
'
' @returns bGoOn - T/F where T means nothing ended the run

' Local Variables:
' @local eSign - SIGN_NEG or SIGN_POS

    bLadderRan := TRUE
    repeat eSign from SIGN_NEG to SIGN_POS
        ceilEnd[eSign] := PO_NOT_RUN
        ceilIncr[eSign] := 0
        resIncr[eSign] := 0
        bResBracketed[eSign] := FALSE
        topCleanIncr[eSign] := 0
        cleanRungs[eSign] := 0
        bCeilFound[eSign] := FALSE
    bGoOn := bSetLimit(rec[REC_LADDER_A])
    repeat eSign from SIGN_NEG to SIGN_POS
        if bGoOn
            bGoOn := bClimb(eSign)
    if bGoOn
        bGoOn := bSetLimit(rec[REC_SCAN_A])

PRI bClimb(eSign) : bGoOn | rungIdx, nIncr, eRo, ePo, bEnded, bResting
' One sign's climb: from rest to the first rung, then a step to each next one; at each, SETTLE_MS and a WINDOW_MS window;
' the climb ends at the first rung whose duty reaches the reserve (clean), at an edge (DROOP, HUNT, CAPPED, FAULT, or a
' drive refused), at a rung the field-step margin forbids (BOUND), or after its last rung (TOP). A ROUGH rung (following
' 3-20 % off, or a re-sync) is left out of the duty line and the climb goes on. Then stopped, and at rest the rungs'
' records, the duty line (ceilingFor()) and MA-CEILING.
'
' @param eSign - SIGN_NEG or SIGN_POS
' @returns bGoOn - T/F where T means nothing ended the run

' Local Variables:
' @local rungIdx - a rung
' @local nIncr - its increment, signed
' @local eRo - its arrival's outcome
' @local ePo - its outcome
' @local bEnded - T/F where T means the climb has ended
' @local bResting - T/F where T means the motor already rests

    bGoOn := TRUE
    bEnded := FALSE
    bResting := FALSE
    ceilEnd[eSign] := END_TOP
    repeat rungIdx from 0 to RUNGS_MAX - 1
        rgOutcome[rungIdx] := PO_NOT_RUN
        rgIncr[rungIdx] := 0
    sampleBegin()
    repeat nRungs with rungIdx
        nIncr := incrForRpm(rec[REC_LADDER_FROM_RPM] + rungIdx * rec[REC_LADDER_STEP_RPM])
        if eSign == SIGN_NEG
            nIncr := -nIncr
        rgIncr[rungIdx] := nIncr
        if bGoOn and (bEnded == FALSE)
            if abs(nIncr) > PK1_CAP_INCR
                rgOutcome[rungIdx] := PO_BOUND
                ceilEnd[eSign] := PO_BOUND
                bEnded := TRUE
            else
                eRo := driveTo(nIncr)
                if eRo == RO_REFUSED
                    ePo := PO_START
                    bResting := TRUE
                elseif eRo == RO_FAULT
                    ePo := PO_FAULT
                elseif eRo == RO_STOPPED
                    ePo := PO_STOPPED
                else
                    ePo := measureRung(rungIdx, nIncr)
                rgOutcome[rungIdx] := ePo
                if ePo == PO_STOPPED
                    bGoOn := FALSE
                    bEnded := TRUE
                elseif ePo == PO_FAULT
                    ceilEnd[eSign] := ePo
                    bEnded := TRUE
                    bResting := TRUE
                    bGoOn := bFaultRecover()
                elseif (ePo == PO_CLEAN) and (rgDuty[rungIdx] * PM >= dutyMax * DUTY_RESERVE_PM)
                    ceilEnd[eSign] := END_RESERVE
                    bEnded := TRUE
                elseif (ePo <> PO_CLEAN) and (ePo <> PO_ROUGH)
                    ceilEnd[eSign] := ePo
                    bEnded := TRUE
        elseif bGoOn
            rgOutcome[rungIdx] := PO_SKIPPED
    if bGoOn and (bResting == FALSE)
        bGoOn := bStopAndRest()
    repeat nRungs with rungIdx
        if rgOutcome[rungIdx] <> PO_NOT_RUN
            emitRung(eSign, rungIdx)
    ceilingFor(eSign)
    emitCeiling(eSign)

PRI measureRung(rungIdx, nIncr) : ePo | eRo
' One rung, arrived (or not in its bound: measured anyway, following says how far short): SETTLE_MS, then a WINDOW_MS
' window, the rung's readings kept and its outcome classified, a duty-capped pass an edge here.
'
' @param rungIdx - the rung
' @param nIncr - its increment, signed
' @returns ePo - PO_CLEAN, PO_ROUGH, PO_DROOP, PO_HUNT, PO_CAPPED, PO_FAULT or PO_STOPPED

' Local Variables:
' @local eRo - the settle's and the window's outcome

    ePo := PO_CLEAN
    windowClear()
    eRo := waitPhase(UNTIL_ELAPSED, 0, SETTLE_MS)
    if eRo == RO_DONE
        windowBegin()
        eRo := waitPhaseWin(WINDOW_MS)
        windowEnd(nIncr)
    if eRo == RO_FAULT
        ePo := PO_FAULT
    elseif eRo == RO_STOPPED
        ePo := PO_STOPPED
    else
        ePo := classify(TRUE)
    rgDuty[rungIdx] := winDuty
    rgFolPm[rungIdx] := winFolPm
    rgDcMa[rungIdx] := winDcMa
    rgHeld[rungIdx] := winHeldD
    rgCapped[rungIdx] := winCapD

PRI ceilingFor(eSign) | rungIdx, nPts, nTop, fSx, fSy, fMx, fMy, fSxx, fSxy, fX, fY, fB, fA, fRes
' The sign's ceiling: the duty line -- least squares of the mean duty against the increment over the clean rungs -- and
' the increment where it reaches DUTY_RESERVE_PM of the duty ceiling; bracketed when that is at or below the fastest
' clean rung. The ceiling is the reserve increment where the climb reached it, else the lesser of it and the fastest
' clean rung (an edge or the field-step margin came first). FOUND (the CEILING check) unless the rungs ran out below the
' reserve (ladder_to too low), the climb never drove, or no rung was clean.
'
' @param eSign - SIGN_NEG or SIGN_POS

' Local Variables:
' @local rungIdx - a rung
' @local nPts - the clean rungs
' @local nTop - the fastest clean rung, increment magnitude
' @local fSx - float sum of the increments
' @local fSy - float sum of the duties
' @local fMx - their mean increment
' @local fMy - their mean duty
' @local fSxx - sum of squared increment deviations
' @local fSxy - sum of increment x duty deviations
' @local fX - one rung's deviation
' @local fY - its duty's
' @local fB - the slope, duty per increment
' @local fA - the intercept, duty
' @local fRes - the reserve increment

    nPts := 0
    nTop := 0
    fSx := fSy := 0.0
    repeat nRungs with rungIdx
        if rgOutcome[rungIdx] == PO_CLEAN
            nPts++
            nTop #>= abs(rgIncr[rungIdx])
            fSx := fSx +. float(abs(rgIncr[rungIdx]))
            fSy := fSy +. float(rgDuty[rungIdx])
    cleanRungs[eSign] := nPts
    topCleanIncr[eSign] := nTop
    if nPts >= 2
        fMx := fSx /. float(nPts)
        fMy := fSy /. float(nPts)
        fSxx := fSxy := 0.0
        repeat nRungs with rungIdx
            if rgOutcome[rungIdx] == PO_CLEAN
                fX := float(abs(rgIncr[rungIdx])) -. fMx
                fY := float(rgDuty[rungIdx]) -. fMy
                fSxx := fSxx +. fX *. fX
                fSxy := fSxy +. fX *. fY
        if fSxx >. 0.0
            fB := fSxy /. fSxx
            fA := fMy -. fB *. fMx
            if fB >. 0.0
                fRes := (float(dutyMax) *. float(DUTY_RESERVE_PM) /. float(PM) -. fA) /. fB
                if fRes >. float(PK1_CAP_INCR)
                    fRes := float(PK1_CAP_INCR)
                if fRes <. 0.0
                    fRes := 0.0
                resIncr[eSign] := round(fRes)
                bResBracketed[eSign] := (resIncr[eSign] <= nTop)
    ceilIncr[eSign] := resIncr[eSign]
    if (ceilEnd[eSign] <> END_RESERVE) and ((resIncr[eSign] == 0) or (nTop < resIncr[eSign]))
        ceilIncr[eSign] := nTop
    bCeilFound[eSign] := (ceilIncr[eSign] > 0) and (ceilEnd[eSign] <> END_TOP) and (ceilEnd[eSign] <> PO_START) and (ceilEnd[eSign] <> PO_STOPPED)

CON { --- the drive: commands, the sampler, the window, recovery --- }

PRI driveTo(nIncr) : eRo
' Command the increment {nIncr} and wait, guarded, until the drive reads AT_SPEED at it, at most ARRIVE_MAX_MS.
'
' @param nIncr - the increment, signed
' @returns eRo - RO_DONE (arrived), RO_TIMEOUT (not in its bound), RO_FAULT, RO_STOPPED or RO_REFUSED (a latched protective stop, cleared)

    if wheel.testDriveAtMotorIncrement(nIncr) <> wheel.NO_ERROR
        eRo := RO_REFUSED
        clearProtect()
    else
        eRo := waitPhase(UNTIL_ARRIVED, nIncr, ARRIVE_MAX_MS)

PRI bStopAndRest() : bGoOn | eRo
' Stop the motor on the built-in ramp (a protective stop already latched has stopped it: cleared first), wait, guarded,
' until it reads STOPPED, then REST_MS. A fault on the way down is cleared; a stop that never comes ends the run.
'
' @returns bGoOn - T/F where T means the motor rests and may be driven

' Local Variables:
' @local eRo - the wait's outcome

    bGoOn := TRUE
    if clearProtect() == wheel.NO_ERROR
        if wheel.testDriveAtMotorIncrement(0) <> wheel.NO_ERROR
            wheel.stopMotor()
    eRo := waitPhase(UNTIL_STOPPED, 0, STOP_MAX_MS)
    if eRo == RO_FAULT
        bGoOn := bFaultRecover()
    elseif eRo == RO_STOPPED
        bGoOn := FALSE
    elseif eRo == RO_TIMEOUT
        coastNow()
        setAbort(AR_STOP_TIMEOUT, smpState)
        bGoOn := FALSE
    else
        waitms(REST_MS)

PRI bFaultRecover() : bGoOn | nStartMs, eOutcome
' After a fault: wait, guarded, until the drive rests (a re-synced fault ramps down; a hard one sits FAULTED), at most
' STOP_MAX_MS; then testResetFault() and a latched protective stop cleared; then REST_MS. A fault that will not clear
' ends the run.
'
' @returns bGoOn - T/F where T means the motor is at rest and may be driven

' Local Variables:
' @local nStartMs - getms() when the wait began
' @local eOutcome - a reading's outcome (GO_FAULT is the fault being recovered: ignored)

    bGoOn := TRUE
    nStartMs := getms()
    repeat
        eOutcome := sampleNext()
        if bGuardStops(eOutcome)
            bGoOn := FALSE
            quit
        if (smpState == wheel.DCS_STOPPED) or (smpState == wheel.DCS_FAULTED) or (getms() - nStartMs >= STOP_MAX_MS)
            quit
    if bGoOn
        bGoOn := (wheel.testResetFault() == wheel.NO_ERROR)
        clearProtect()
        if bGoOn
            waitms(REST_MS)
        else
            coastNow()
            setAbort(AR_FAULT_STUCK, smpState)

PRI clearProtect() : eProt
' Clear a latched protective stop (a drive it refuses would leave the tool unable to drive), returning its cause.
'
' @returns eProt - the cause latched; NO_ERROR when none

    eProt := wheel.getProtectiveStop()
    if eProt <> wheel.NO_ERROR
        wheel.clearProtectiveStop()

PRI coastNow()
' Coast the motor at once by stopping its driver: every guard that ends the run comes through here.

    benchLog.cogEventBegin()
    wheel.stop()

PRI sampleBegin()
' Start the sampler: its first reading SAMPLE_MS from now, the abort's run of readings cleared.

    smpPeriodCt := clkfreq / wheel.MS_PER_SEC * SAMPLE_MS
    smpNextCt := getct() + smpPeriodCt
    overSamples := 0

PRI sampleNext() : eOutcome
' Wait for the next reading's time (a busy wait on getct(): no waitct() can wrap), read the drive, and judge the guards
' (judgeGuards()). A reading more than a period late is taken at once and the cadence re-anchored.
'
' @returns eOutcome - GO_RUNNING; GO_FAULT (a finding); or the guard's GO_* that ends the run

    repeat until getct() - smpNextCt >= 0
    if getct() - smpNextCt >= smpPeriodCt
        smpNextCt := getct()
    smpNextCt += smpPeriodCt
    smpCt := getct()
    smpMs := getms()
    smpDuty, _, smpSenseMv, _, _, _, smpState, bSmpFault := wheel.testGetTelemetry()
    smpHeld, smpCapped, smpDrvIncr, smpPos := wheel.testGetDriveHealth()
    eOutcome := judgeGuards()

PRI judgeGuards() : eOutcome | nNetMa
' Integrate the charge and judge every run-ending guard from the latest reading -- the absolute abort, the charge cap,
' the time cap -- then the fault, a finding.
'
' @returns eOutcome - GO_RUNNING, GO_FAULT, or the GO_* that ends the run

' Local Variables:
' @local nNetMa - the reading net of the rest zero, mA

    eOutcome := GO_RUNNING
    nNetMa := netMilliamps(smpSenseMv)
    chargeSamples += nNetMa
    peakMa #>= nNetMa
    overSamples := (nNetMa >= abortMa) ? overSamples + 1 : 0
    if overSamples >= ABS_ABORT_SAMPLES
        eOutcome := GO_OVER_CURRENT
    elseif chargeSamples >= chargeCapSamples
        eOutcome := GO_CHARGE_CAP
    elseif getms() - runStartMs >= timeCapMs
        eOutcome := GO_TIME_CAP
    elseif bSmpFault
        eOutcome := GO_FAULT

PRI bGuardStops(eOutcome) : bStops
' Whether a reading's outcome ends the run -- anything but GO_RUNNING and GO_FAULT -- and, when it does, coast the
' motor at once and record why.
'
' @param eOutcome - sampleNext()'s outcome
' @returns bStops - T/F where T means the run ends now

    bStops := (eOutcome <> GO_RUNNING) and (eOutcome <> GO_FAULT)
    if bStops
        coastNow()
        case eOutcome
            GO_OVER_CURRENT:    setAbort(AR_OVER_CURRENT, peakMa)
            GO_CHARGE_CAP:      setAbort(AR_CHARGE_CAP, chargeSamples / SAMPLES_PER_SEC)
            other:              setAbort(AR_TIME_CAP, (getms() - runStartMs) / wheel.MS_PER_SEC)

PRI waitPhase(eUntil, nTarget, nBoundMs) : eRo | nStartMs, eOutcome, bHeld
' Take readings until the condition {eUntil} holds, the driver faults, a guard ends the run, or {nBoundMs} passes.
'
' @param eUntil - UNTIL_ARRIVED, UNTIL_STOPPED or UNTIL_ELAPSED
' @param nTarget - UNTIL_ARRIVED's increment, signed; unused otherwise
' @param nBoundMs - the bound, ms (UNTIL_ELAPSED: the phase's length)
' @returns eRo - RO_DONE (UNTIL_ELAPSED: the time passed), RO_TIMEOUT, RO_FAULT or RO_STOPPED

' Local Variables:
' @local nStartMs - getms() at the call
' @local eOutcome - a reading's outcome
' @local bHeld - T/F where T means the condition holds at this reading

    nStartMs := getms()
    eRo := RO_TIMEOUT
    repeat
        eOutcome := sampleNext()
        if eOutcome == GO_FAULT
            eRo := RO_FAULT
            quit
        if bGuardStops(eOutcome)
            eRo := RO_STOPPED
            quit
        bHeld := FALSE
        if eUntil == UNTIL_ARRIVED
            bHeld := (smpState == wheel.DCS_AT_SPEED) and (smpDrvIncr == nTarget)
        elseif eUntil == UNTIL_STOPPED
            bHeld := (smpState == wheel.DCS_STOPPED)
        if bHeld
            eRo := RO_DONE
            quit
        if smpMs - nStartMs >= nBoundMs
            if eUntil == UNTIL_ELAPSED
                eRo := RO_DONE
            quit

PRI waitPhaseWin(nLenMs) : eRo | nStartMs, eOutcome
' Take readings for {nLenMs}, each added to the open window.
'
' @param nLenMs - the window's length, ms
' @returns eRo - RO_DONE, RO_FAULT or RO_STOPPED

' Local Variables:
' @local nStartMs - the window's start, getms()
' @local eOutcome - a reading's outcome

    eRo := RO_DONE
    nStartMs := smpMs
    repeat
        eOutcome := sampleNext()
        windowAdd()
        if eOutcome == GO_FAULT
            eRo := RO_FAULT
            quit
        if bGuardStops(eOutcome)
            eRo := RO_STOPPED
            quit
        if smpMs - nStartMs >= nLenMs
            quit

PRI windowClear()
' Empty the window's results: a point or rung that ends before its window keeps zeros.

    winN := winSenseSum := winDutySum := 0
    winDcMa := winDuty := winFolPm := winHeldD := winCapD := winResyncD := 0

PRI windowBegin()
' Open a measuring window at the latest reading: its counters and its hall position, and empty sums.

    windowClear()
    winPos0 := smpPos
    winHeld0 := smpHeld
    winCap0 := smpCapped
    winCt0 := smpCt
    _, _, winResync0 := wheel.testGetFaultResponse()

PRI windowAdd()
' Add the latest reading to the open window.

    winN++
    winSenseSum += smpSenseMv
    winDutySum += smpDuty

PRI windowEnd(nIncr) | nResync, nDct, fCmdTps, fMeasTps
' Close the window: the DC link's mean through the board's scale, the mean duty, the held and capped passes and the
' re-synced faults over it, and the following -- the halls' speed over the window against the speed {nIncr} commands
' (|incr| x 6 hall ticks per 2^32 x the drive's pass rate), per mille.
'
' @param nIncr - the increment commanded, signed

' Local Variables:
' @local nResync - the re-synced faults since start, now
' @local nDct - the window's clocks (at most 5 s: under a signed getct() difference at 350 MHz)
' @local fCmdTps - the commanded hall ticks per second
' @local fMeasTps - the measured hall ticks per second

    _, _, nResync := wheel.testGetFaultResponse()
    winResyncD := nResync - winResync0
    winHeldD := smpHeld - winHeld0
    winCapD := smpCapped - winCap0
    winDcMa := 0
    winDuty := 0
    if winN > 0
        winDcMa := divRound((divRound(winSenseSum * X100, winN) - zeroMvX10 * X10) * X10, mvPerA #> 1)
        winDuty := divRound(winDutySum, winN)
    winFolPm := 0
    nDct := smpCt - winCt0
    fCmdTps := float(abs(nIncr)) *. float(wheel.HALL_TICKS_PER_CYCLE * wheel.PWM_RATE_IN_HZ) /. (float(wheel.DRIVE_PASS_FRAMES) *. F_2POW32)
    if (nDct > 0) and (fCmdTps >. 0.0)
        fMeasTps := float(abs(smpPos - winPos0)) *. float(clkfreq) /. float(nDct)
        winFolPm := clampedRound(fMeasTps /. fCmdTps *. float(PM), LIM_MID)

PRI netMilliamps(nSenseMv) : nNetMa
' A current-sense reading net of the rest zero, in mA of DC link through the detected board's scale.
'
' @param nSenseMv - the reading, mV
' @returns nNetMa - the net current, mA

    nNetMa := divRound((nSenseMv * X10 - zeroMvX10) * X100, mvPerA #> 1)

PRI incrForRpm(nRpm) : nIncr
' The drive law inverted: the increment for {nRpm} on this motor (ticks_rev hall ticks a revolution, 6 a cycle, 2^32 a
' cycle, the drive's pass rate).
'
' @param nRpm - rpm, at least 0
' @returns nIncr - the increment, positive

    nIncr := muldiv64(nRpm * rec[REC_TICKS_PER_REV] * wheel.DRIVE_PASS_FRAMES * 2, $8000_0000, SECS_PER_MIN * wheel.HALL_TICKS_PER_CYCLE * wheel.PWM_RATE_IN_HZ)

PRI rpmX10ForIncr(nIncr) : nRpmX10
' The drive law: an increment's speed on this motor, tenths of an rpm.
'
' @param nIncr - the increment, either sign
' @returns nRpmX10 - tenths of an rpm

    nRpmX10 := clampedRound(float(abs(nIncr)) *. float(SECS_PER_MIN * X10 * wheel.HALL_TICKS_PER_CYCLE * wheel.PWM_RATE_IN_HZ) /. (float(rec[REC_TICKS_PER_REV] * wheel.DRIVE_PASS_FRAMES) *. F_2POW32), LIM_MID)

CON { --- arithmetic --- }

PRI divRound(nNumerator, nDenominator) : nQuotient
' {nNumerator} / {nDenominator} rounded half away from zero ("/" truncates toward zero).
'
' @param nNumerator - any value
' @param nDenominator - above 0
' @returns nQuotient - the rounded quotient

    if nNumerator >= 0
        nQuotient := (nNumerator + nDenominator / 2) / nDenominator
    else
        nQuotient := (nNumerator - nDenominator / 2) / nDenominator

PRI wrapPositive(nValue, nModulus) : nWrapped
' {nValue} modulo {nModulus} in 0 .. nModulus - 1 ("//" keeps the dividend's sign).
'
' @param nValue - any value
' @param nModulus - the modulus, above 0
' @returns nWrapped - the value in 0 .. nModulus - 1

    nWrapped := nValue // nModulus
    if nWrapped < 0
        nWrapped += nModulus

PRI wrapSigned(nValue, nModulus) : nWrapped
' {nValue} modulo {nModulus} in -nModulus / 2 .. nModulus / 2.
'
' @param nValue - any value
' @param nModulus - the modulus, above 0
' @returns nWrapped - the value in -nModulus / 2 .. nModulus / 2

    nWrapped := wrapPositive(nValue, nModulus)
    if nWrapped > nModulus / 2
        nWrapped -= nModulus

PRI clampedRound(fValue, nLimit) : nValue
' A float rounded to the nearest integer, clamped to +-{nLimit} first (round() of a float past a long is undefined).
'
' @param fValue - the float
' @param nLimit - the clamp, above 0
' @returns nValue - the rounded, clamped value

    nValue := nLimit
    if fValue <. float(nLimit)
        nValue := -nLimit
        if fValue >. float(-nLimit)
            nValue := round(fValue)

PRI setAbort(eReason, nDetail)
' Record why the run ended early: the first cause is kept.
'
' @param eReason - AR_*
' @param nDetail - its detail

    if eAbortReason == AR_NONE
        eAbortReason := eReason
        abortDetail := nDetail

PRI refuse(eReason, nDetail)
' Refuse the run before anything is started: record why and emit MA-REFUSE.
'
' @param eReason - AR_*
' @param nDetail - its detail (the motor type, the record's format, the driver's ticks, a count)

    setAbort(eReason, nDetail)
    benchLog.begin(@"MA-REFUSE")
    benchLog.tokenField(@"reason", abortToken(eReason), TOKMAX)
    benchLog.numField(@"detail", nDetail, LIM_BIG)
    benchLog.numField(@"motor_type", user.MOTOR_TYPE, LIM_TINY)
    lineEmit()

CON { --- records --- }

PRI emitBanner()
' Emit MA-BANNER: the tool, its formats, what it was built for, the clock.

    benchLog.begin(@"MA-BANNER")
    benchLog.numField(@"tool_rev", TOOL_REV, LIM_TINY)
    benchLog.numField(@"fmt", FMT_VERSION, LIM_TINY)
    benchLog.numField(@"record_fmt", RECORD_FORMAT, LIM_TINY)
    benchLog.tokenField(@"build", buildToken(), TOKMAX)
    benchLog.numField(@"clk_hz", clkfreq, LIM_BIG)
    lineEmit()

PRI emitRecord(bFound)
' Emit MA-RECORD: the record found for the configured motor type, every field; NA throughout when there is none.
'
' @param bFound - T/F where T means a record was found

    benchLog.begin(@"MA-RECORD")
    benchLog.boolField(@"found", bFound)
    benchLog.numField(@"motor_type", user.MOTOR_TYPE, LIM_TINY)
    benchLog.naNumField(@"format", rec[REC_FORMAT], LIM_TINY, bFound)
    if bFound
        benchLog.tokenField(@"status", statusToken(rec[REC_STATUS]), TOKMAX)
    else
        benchLog.textField(@"status", @sNaTok)
    benchLog.naNumField(@"ticks_rev", rec[REC_TICKS_PER_REV], LIM_SMALL, bFound)
    benchLog.naNumField(@"rated_ma", rec[REC_RATED_MA], LIM_MID, bFound)
    benchLog.naNumField(@"no_load_ma", rec[REC_NO_LOAD_MA], LIM_MID, bFound)
    benchLog.naNumField(@"scan_a", rec[REC_SCAN_A], LIM_TINY, bFound)
    benchLog.naNumField(@"ladder_a", rec[REC_LADDER_A], LIM_TINY, bFound)
    benchLog.naNumField(@"slow_rpm", rec[REC_SLOW_RPM], LIM_MID, bFound)
    benchLog.naNumField(@"fast_rpm", rec[REC_FAST_RPM], LIM_MID, bFound)
    benchLog.naNumField(@"ladder_from_rpm", rec[REC_LADDER_FROM_RPM], LIM_MID, bFound)
    benchLog.naNumField(@"ladder_step_rpm", rec[REC_LADDER_STEP_RPM], LIM_MID, bFound)
    benchLog.naNumField(@"ladder_to_rpm", rec[REC_LADDER_TO_RPM], LIM_MID, bFound)
    lineEmit()

PRI emitPoint(eSpeed, eSign, slotIdx)
' Emit MA-POINT: one offset-scan point. At rest.
'
' @param eSpeed - SPEED_SLOW or SPEED_FAST
' @param eSign - SIGN_NEG or SIGN_POS
' @param slotIdx - the point's slot

    benchLog.begin(@"MA-POINT")
    benchLog.numField(@"rpm", rec[REC_SLOW_RPM + eSpeed], LIM_MID)
    benchLog.tokenField(@"sign", signToken(eSign), TOKMAX)
    benchLog.tokenField(@"side", sideToken(slotIdx / OFS_SIDE_POINTS), TOKMAX)
    benchLog.numField(@"d", ptD[slotIdx], LIM_TINY)
    benchLog.numField(@"deg", ptDeg[slotIdx], LIM_TINY)
    benchLog.tokenField(@"outcome", outcomeToken(ptOutcome[slotIdx]), TOKMAX)
    benchLog.numField(@"dc_ma", ptDcMa[slotIdx], LIM_MID)
    benchLog.numField(@"duty", ptDuty[slotIdx], LIM_MID)
    benchLog.numField(@"fol_pm", ptFolPm[slotIdx], LIM_MID)
    benchLog.numField(@"held", ptHeld[slotIdx], LIM_MID)
    benchLog.numField(@"capped", ptCapped[slotIdx], LIM_MID)
    benchLog.numField(@"resyncs", ptResyncs[slotIdx], LIM_SMALL)
    lineEmit()

PRI emitSide(eSpeed, eSign, eSide) | slotIdx, nRun
' Emit MA-SIDE: how one side of the scan ended, and the points it ran.
'
' @param eSpeed - SPEED_SLOW or SPEED_FAST
' @param eSign - SIGN_NEG or SIGN_POS
' @param eSide - SIDE_PLUS or SIDE_MINUS

' Local Variables:
' @local slotIdx - a point's slot
' @local nRun - the side's points that ran

    nRun := 0
    repeat slotIdx from eSide * OFS_SIDE_POINTS to eSide * OFS_SIDE_POINTS + OFS_SIDE_STEPS
        if (ptOutcome[slotIdx] <> PO_NOT_RUN) and (ptOutcome[slotIdx] <> PO_SKIPPED)
            nRun++
    benchLog.begin(@"MA-SIDE")
    benchLog.numField(@"rpm", rec[REC_SLOW_RPM + eSpeed], LIM_MID)
    benchLog.tokenField(@"sign", signToken(eSign), TOKMAX)
    benchLog.tokenField(@"side", sideToken(eSide), TOKMAX)
    benchLog.tokenField(@"end", outcomeToken(sideEnd[eSide]), TOKMAX)
    benchLog.numField(@"points", nRun, LIM_TINY)
    lineEmit()

PRI emitFit(eSpeed, eSign, spIdx)
' Emit MA-FIT: one speed and sign's current minimum -- resolved or not, from the start pair and absolute, its error.
'
' @param eSpeed - SPEED_SLOW or SPEED_FAST
' @param eSign - SIGN_NEG or SIGN_POS
' @param spIdx - the fit slot

    benchLog.begin(@"MA-FIT")
    benchLog.numField(@"rpm", rec[REC_SLOW_RPM + eSpeed], LIM_MID)
    benchLog.tokenField(@"sign", signToken(eSign), TOKMAX)
    benchLog.boolField(@"resolved", bFitOk[spIdx])
    benchLog.numField(@"pts", fitPts[spIdx], LIM_TINY)
    benchLog.numField(@"start_deg", startOffset(eSign), LIM_SMALL)
    benchLog.numField(@"from_start_x10", fitFromX10[spIdx], LIM_SMALL)
    benchLog.numField(@"deg_x10", fitAbsX10[spIdx], LIM_SMALL)
    benchLog.numField(@"se_x10", fitSeX10[spIdx], LIM_SMALL)
    benchLog.numField(@"se_max_x10", VERT_SE_MAX_X10, LIM_SMALL)
    lineEmit()

PRI emitRung(eSign, rungIdx)
' Emit MA-RUNG: one ladder rung. At rest.
'
' @param eSign - SIGN_NEG or SIGN_POS
' @param rungIdx - the rung

    benchLog.begin(@"MA-RUNG")
    benchLog.tokenField(@"sign", signToken(eSign), TOKMAX)
    benchLog.numField(@"rpm_x10", rpmX10ForIncr(rgIncr[rungIdx]), LIM_MID)
    benchLog.numField(@"incr", rgIncr[rungIdx], LIM_BIG)
    benchLog.tokenField(@"outcome", outcomeToken(rgOutcome[rungIdx]), TOKMAX)
    benchLog.numField(@"duty", rgDuty[rungIdx], LIM_MID)
    benchLog.numField(@"duty_pm", divRound(rgDuty[rungIdx] * PM, dutyMax #> 1), LIM_MID)
    benchLog.numField(@"fol_pm", rgFolPm[rungIdx], LIM_MID)
    benchLog.numField(@"dc_ma", rgDcMa[rungIdx], LIM_MID)
    benchLog.numField(@"held", rgHeld[rungIdx], LIM_MID)
    benchLog.numField(@"capped", rgCapped[rungIdx], LIM_MID)
    lineEmit()

PRI emitCeiling(eSign)
' Emit MA-CEILING: one sign's climb -- how it ended, its duty line's reserve increment, whether that is bracketed, and the
' ceiling.
'
' @param eSign - SIGN_NEG or SIGN_POS

    benchLog.begin(@"MA-CEILING")
    benchLog.tokenField(@"sign", signToken(eSign), TOKMAX)
    benchLog.tokenField(@"end", outcomeToken(ceilEnd[eSign]), TOKMAX)
    benchLog.boolField(@"found", bCeilFound[eSign])
    benchLog.numField(@"clean", cleanRungs[eSign], LIM_TINY)
    benchLog.naNumField(@"reserve_incr", resIncr[eSign], LIM_BIG, resIncr[eSign] > 0)
    benchLog.boolField(@"bracketed", bResBracketed[eSign])
    benchLog.numField(@"top_clean_incr", topCleanIncr[eSign], LIM_BIG)
    benchLog.naNumField(@"ceil_incr", ceilIncr[eSign], LIM_BIG, ceilIncr[eSign] > 0)
    benchLog.naNumField(@"ceil_rpm_x10", rpmX10ForIncr(ceilIncr[eSign]), LIM_MID, ceilIncr[eSign] > 0)
    benchLog.numField(@"reserve_pm", DUTY_RESERVE_PM, LIM_SMALL)
    benchLog.numField(@"duty_max", dutyMax, LIM_MID)
    lineEmit()

PRI emitResult() | nCeil, bCeil, bZ
' Emit MA-RESULT: what to put in the driver for this motor at this voltage -- the pair at each scan speed (for
' offsetsForMotor()), Z and its check, and the ceiling (for confgurePowerLimits(): the lesser of the two signs', found
' when both signs found one; how each climb ended is in its MA-CEILING).

' Local Variables:
' @local nCeil - the ceiling, increment magnitude
' @local bCeil - T/F where T means both signs found a ceiling
' @local bZ - T/F where T means at least one speed's pair resolved

    bCeil := bLadderRan and bCeilFound[SIGN_NEG] and bCeilFound[SIGN_POS]
    nCeil := ceilIncr[SIGN_NEG] <# ceilIncr[SIGN_POS]
    bZ := bScanRan and (bPairOk[SPEED_SLOW] or bPairOk[SPEED_FAST])
    benchLog.begin(@"MA-RESULT")
    if bRecordFound
        benchLog.tokenField(@"record", statusToken(rec[REC_STATUS]), TOKMAX)
    else
        benchLog.textField(@"record", @sNaTok)
    benchLog.naNumField(@"told_mv", toldMv, LIM_MID, toldMv > 0)
    benchLog.naNumField(@"z_x10", (bPairOk[SPEED_SLOW] ? zX10[SPEED_SLOW] : zX10[SPEED_FAST]), LIM_SMALL, bZ)
    benchLog.tokenField(@"z_check", verdictToken(eZVerdict), TOKMAX)
    benchLog.naNumField(@"slow_fwd_deg", degreesOf(fitAbsX10[SPEED_SLOW * SIGNS + SIGN_NEG]), LIM_SMALL, bScanRan and bPairOk[SPEED_SLOW])
    benchLog.naNumField(@"slow_rev_deg", degreesOf(fitAbsX10[SPEED_SLOW * SIGNS + SIGN_POS]), LIM_SMALL, bScanRan and bPairOk[SPEED_SLOW])
    benchLog.naNumField(@"fast_fwd_deg", degreesOf(fitAbsX10[SPEED_FAST * SIGNS + SIGN_NEG]), LIM_SMALL, bScanRan and bPairOk[SPEED_FAST])
    benchLog.naNumField(@"fast_rev_deg", degreesOf(fitAbsX10[SPEED_FAST * SIGNS + SIGN_POS]), LIM_SMALL, bScanRan and bPairOk[SPEED_FAST])
    benchLog.tokenField(@"ceil_lead", leadToken(bStartBySpeed), TOKMAX)
    benchLog.boolField(@"ceil_found", bCeil)
    benchLog.naNumField(@"ceil_incr", nCeil, LIM_BIG, bLadderRan and (nCeil > 0))
    benchLog.naNumField(@"ceil_rpm_x10", rpmX10ForIncr(nCeil), LIM_MID, bLadderRan and (nCeil > 0))
    lineEmit()

PRI emitEnd()
' Emit MA-END: why the run ended (NONE: it ran to the end), its length, its charge and its peak current.

    benchLog.begin(@"MA-END")
    benchLog.tokenField(@"stopped", abortToken(eAbortReason), TOKMAX)
    benchLog.numField(@"detail", abortDetail, LIM_BIG)
    benchLog.numField(@"run_s", (getms() - runStartMs) / wheel.MS_PER_SEC, LIM_MID)
    benchLog.numField(@"charge_mas", chargeSamples / SAMPLES_PER_SEC, LIM_BIG)
    benchLog.numField(@"peak_ma", peakMa, LIM_MID)
    lineEmit()

PRI lineEmit()
' Emit the assembled record: the one debug() statement every record goes through.

    debug(zstr_(benchLog.pLine()))

CON { --- tokens --- }

PRI signToken(eSign) : pToken
' The token for an increment sign.
'
' @param eSign - SIGN_NEG or SIGN_POS
' @returns pToken - NEG or POS

    pToken := @sPosTok
    if eSign == SIGN_NEG
        pToken := @sNegTok

PRI sideToken(eSide) : pToken
' The token for a side of the start pair.
'
' @param eSide - SIDE_PLUS or SIDE_MINUS
' @returns pToken - PLUS or MINUS

    pToken := @sMinusTok
    if eSide == SIDE_PLUS
        pToken := @sPlusTok

PRI leadToken(bBySpeed) : pToken
' The token for how the driver sets the pair.
'
' @param bBySpeed - T/F where T means by speed (the lead table)
' @returns pToken - BY_SPEED or FIXED

    pToken := @sFixedTok
    if bBySpeed
        pToken := @sSpeedTok

PRI statusToken(eStatus) : pToken
' The token for a record's status.
'
' @param eStatus - RS_MEASURED or RS_PROVISIONAL
' @returns pToken - MEASURED, PROVISIONAL, or NA for anything else

    case eStatus
        RS_MEASURED:    pToken := @sMeasuredTok
        RS_PROVISIONAL: pToken := @sProvisTok
        other:          pToken := @sNaTok

PRI verdictToken(eVerdict) : pToken
' The token for a check's verdict.
'
' @param eVerdict - VD_*
' @returns pToken - PASS, FAIL or NA

    case eVerdict
        VD_PASS:        pToken := @sPassTok
        VD_FAIL:        pToken := @sFailTok
        other:          pToken := @sNaTok

PRI boardToken(eRevision) : pToken
' The token for a board revision.
'
' @param eRevision - REV_A, REV_B or REV_Unknown
' @returns pToken - REV_A, REV_B or UNKNOWN

    case eRevision
        wheel.REV_A:    pToken := @sRevATok
        wheel.REV_B:    pToken := @sRevBTok
        other:          pToken := @sUnknownTok

PRI buildToken() : pToken
' The token for what this image was built for.
'
' @returns pToken - USER, DOCO_BENCH or WHEEL_BENCH

    case BUILD_KIND
        BUILD_DOCO_BENCH:   pToken := @sDocoTok
        BUILD_WHEEL_BENCH:  pToken := @sWheelTok
        other:              pToken := @sUserTok

PRI outcomeToken(eOutcome) : pToken
' The token for a point's or rung's outcome, or a side's or climb's end.
'
' @param eOutcome - PO_* or END_*
' @returns pToken - its token; NA for anything else

    case eOutcome
        PO_NOT_RUN:     pToken := @sNotRunTok
        PO_SKIPPED:     pToken := @sSkippedTok
        PO_CLEAN:       pToken := @sCleanTok
        PO_ROUGH:       pToken := @sRoughTok
        PO_DROOP:       pToken := @sDroopTok
        PO_HUNT:        pToken := @sHuntTok
        PO_CAPPED:      pToken := @sCappedTok
        PO_WALL:        pToken := @sWallTok
        PO_FAULT:       pToken := @sFaultTok
        PO_STOPPED:     pToken := @sStoppedTok
        PO_START:       pToken := @sStartTok
        PO_BOUND:       pToken := @sBoundTok
        END_LIMIT:      pToken := @sLimitTok
        END_RESERVE:    pToken := @sReserveTok
        END_TOP:        pToken := @sTopTok
        END_BRACKETED:  pToken := @sBracketTok
        other:          pToken := @sNaTok

PRI abortToken(eReason) : pToken
' The token for why the run ended early, or was refused.
'
' @param eReason - AR_*
' @returns pToken - its token; NA for anything else

    case eReason
        AR_NONE:            pToken := @sNoneTok
        AR_NO_RECORD:       pToken := @sNoRecordTok
        AR_RECORD_FORMAT:   pToken := @sRecFormatTok
        AR_GEOMETRY:        pToken := @sGeometryTok
        AR_RECORD_PLAN:     pToken := @sRecPlanTok
        AR_CONFIG:          pToken := @sConfigTok
        AR_START:           pToken := @sStartTok
        AR_BOARD:           pToken := @sBoardTok
        AR_LIMIT:           pToken := @sLimitTok
        AR_ZERO:            pToken := @sZeroTok
        AR_OVER_CURRENT:    pToken := @sOverTok
        AR_CHARGE_CAP:      pToken := @sChargeTok
        AR_TIME_CAP:        pToken := @sTimeTok
        AR_FAULT_STUCK:     pToken := @sFaultStuckTok
        AR_STOP_TIMEOUT:    pToken := @sStopTimeTok
        AR_RESTORE:         pToken := @sRestoreTok
        other:              pToken := @sNaTok

